hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7801","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ishkab narrated to us, Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah al-Majishun narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl who said: Suwayd ibn Ghaflah, Zayd ibn Suham, and a third with them were on a journey. One of them found a whip and took it. His two companions said to him: Throw it away. He said: I will use it; if its owner comes I will give it to him, better than leaving it for beasts to devour. He met Ubayy ibn Kab and mentioned that to him, and he said: You were right and they were wrong. He said: I found a hundred dinars in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I brought them to him. He said: Announce it for a year. I announced it and it was not recognized. I returned to him and he said: Announce it for a year. I announced it for a year and it was not recognized, twice or thrice. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Know its count, its container, and its tie; mix it with your wealth, and if its owner comes, give it to him. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl except Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah; Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna is alone in transmitting it."
"7802","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, who said: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, Imran ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father Muhammad ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor has more right to his adjoining property, whatever it is. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Ibn Abi Layla; Imran ibn Muhammad is alone in transmitting it."
"7803","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Dawud al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Said al-Khudri: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted cupping for the fasting person. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Ishaq al-Azraq."
"7804","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, Murajja ibn Raja narrated to us, Abu Rayhanah narrated to us, from Safinah who said: I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ten years; he would bathe with a sa and perform ablution with a mudd. No one narrated this hadith from Murajja ibn Raja except Yaqub al-Hadrami."
"7805","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu Shuayb narrating from Muhammad ibn Sirin and Anas ibn Sirin and Nafi, that they narrated to him, from Ibn Umar who said: I memorized ten prayers from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): two before noon, two after it, two after Maghrib, two after Isha, and two before dawn. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Shuayb, who is al-Salt ibn Dinar, except Mutamir."
"7806","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, who said: Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nashai narrated to us, Silah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs pilgrimage on behalf of his parents, or settles a debt on their behalf, Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection with the righteous. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Silah ibn Sulayman; Muhammad ibn Harb is alone in transmitting it."
"7807","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, Umayr ibn Imran narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you begins prayer, let him raise his hands and face their palms toward the qiblah, for Allah is before him."
"7808","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, Umayr narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is in the mosque, let him not make anyone hear his voice; let him point with his finger to his Lord, blessed and exalted. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ibn Jurayj except Umayr ibn Imran; Muhammad ibn Harb is alone in transmitting them."
"7809","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Umar ibn Yunus narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Ijli Abu Muhammad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, from Hanzalah ibn Qays, from Rafi ibn Khadij who said: What the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us of land lease was that a man leases his land on condition that whatever is pointed to is his; this was what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Umar ibn Yunus."
"7810","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Umar ibn Yunus al-Yamami narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When this verse was revealed it weighed upon the Muslims, and they deemed it grave that twenty fight two hundred and a hundred a thousand. Allah lightened it for them and abrogated it with the verse after it: Now Allah has lightened for you, knowing there is weakness in you; if there are a hundred steadfast among you they will overcome two hundred, and if there are a thousand among you they will overcome two thousand by the permission of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Yunus ibn al-Qasim; his son is alone in transmitting it."
"7811","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abu Salamah Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Amrah, from Aisha, and from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aisha, who said: The verse of stoning and of ten sucklings of the adult was revealed; it was in a sheet under my bed. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died and we were occupied with his death, a tame sheep entered and ate it. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim except Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"7812","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, Silah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Awf, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the night I was taken, I passed by Musa while he was standing praying in his grave at the red dune. No one narrated this hadith from Awf except Silah ibn Sulayman; Muhammad ibn Harb is alone in transmitting it."
"7813","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nashai narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, from Abu al-Awwam Imran al-Qattan, from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear the waist-wrapper as you saw the angels wear it. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how did you see? He said: To the middle of their shins. No one narrated this hadith from Imran al-Qattan except Yahya ibn al-Sakan."
"7814","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Umar ibn Rashid, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: It is the right of a Muslim not to spend two nights without writing his will, if he has something to bequeath. No one narrated this hadith from Umar ibn Rashid except Ubaydah."
"7815","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out with a piece of gold in his hand and a piece of silk and said: These two are forbidden for the males of my nation and permitted for its females. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Ismail ibn Muslim."
"7816","Mahmud narrated to us, Jafar ibn Abdullah ibn Mahmud Abu Muhammad al-Warraq al-Wasiti narrated to us, Hanan ibn Sadyr al-Sayrafi narrated to us, who said: I heard Ibn al-Ghasil say: An uncle of mine called Amr ibn Sahl narrated to me, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Kinship increases wealth, love among family, and postponement of the term. No one narrated this hadith from Hanan ibn Sadyr except Abu Muhammad, and it is not narrated from Amr ibn Sahl except with this chain."
"7817","Mahmud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thalabah ibn Sawa narrated to us, my uncle Muhammad ibn Sawa narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jarhad, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by his father while he was uncovering his thigh, and said: Cover it, for it is part of nakedness. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Mamar, nor from Mamar except Said; Muhammad ibn Sawa is alone in transmitting it."
"7818","Mahmud narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Salim, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father who said: I attended a funeral with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he intended to pray over it, he turned and saw a woman, so he ordered her driven away until he no longer saw her, then he stepped forward and said takbir over it four times. No one narrated this hadith from Salamah ibn Kuhayl except Muhammad ibn Salim, nor from Muhammad except Ubaydah; Zahmawayh is alone in transmitting it."
"7819","Mahmud narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: Maiz ibn Malik came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have committed adultery. He turned away from him, then he came to him and said: I have committed adultery. He turned away from him until he came to him four times. Then he ordered him stoned. When the stones struck him he fled running; a man met him and threw at him a camel's jawbone and felled him. His fleeing when the stones touched him was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Would that you had left him. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Abbad."
"7820","Mahmud narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, al-Rabi ibn Badr narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting is a shield, so long as he does not tear it. He said: It was said: What tears it? He said: With a lie or with backbiting. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except al-Rabi ibn Badr."
"7821","Mahmud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ibn Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from his father, from Thawban, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be upright toward Quraysh so long as they are upright toward you; if they do not, put your swords upon your necks and annihilate their multitude; if you do not, be toiling farmers, eating the toil of your hands. None said in this hadith, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ibn Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from his father, except Khalid; Muhammad ibn Khalid is alone in transmitting it. People narrated it from Yazid, from Salim."
"7822","Mahmud narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, Bishr ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah cursed wine, its drinker, its pourer, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its seller, the eater of its price, and its buyer."
"7823","Mahmud narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, Bishr narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be cupped at this cupping on the front of his head, and he called it Umm Mughith. No one narrated these two hadiths from Nafi except Abd al-Aziz, nor from Abd al-Aziz except Bishr; Zahmawayh is alone in transmitting them."
"7824","Mahmud narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from Fatimah bint Qays, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the woman with prolonged bleeding. He said: She counts the days of her menses, then she bathes at every purification, then she packs and prays. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Jafar ibn Sulayman."
"7825","Mahmud narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Amr ibn Yahya, from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Anas ibn Malik who said: There were not twenty white hairs in the head and beard of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Yahya except Khalid."
"7826","Mahmud narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abdullah al-Bakkai narrated to us, Idris al-Awdi narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father who said: Bilal called the adhan for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in pairs, and the iqamah likewise. No one narrated this hadith from Idris except Ziyad ibn Abdullah."
"7827","Mahmud narrated to us, Bishr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar al-Qattan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, Shamlah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Umar ibn Shaybah ibn Abi Kathir al-Ashjai, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The flushing of the face from nabidh scatters good deeds. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; al-Waqidi is alone in transmitting it."
"7828","Mahmud narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us, from Wasil, the freedman of Abu Uyaynah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us in an army and appointed over us Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. Our provisions ran out, so we came to the seashore, and there we found a creature like a dune cast up by the sea. We secured it, ate, and took provisions. We mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: It is game Allah fed you with. No one narrated this hadith from Wasil except Khalid."
"7829","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Sinan ibn Harun narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he said at his death: I grieve over nothing I missed of the world except three: fasting in the midday heats, not parting my feet in prayer, meaning lengthy prayer, and my resignation over the pledge. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Muhammad ibn Ishaq, nor from Muhammad except Sinan ibn Harun; Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh is alone in transmitting it."
"7830","Mahmud narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Aban al-Muallim, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman used to begin recitation with Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. No one narrated this hadith from Aban al-Muallim except Khalid."
"7831","Mahmud narrated to us, Zakariyya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Sinan ibn Harun narrated from al-Hasan ibn Amr, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see my ummah fearing to say to the oppressor: you are an oppressor, then they have been abandoned. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Amr from Abu al-Zubayr except Sinan; Zahmawayh is alone in it."
"7832","Mahmud narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa al-Sinani narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from Usamah ibn Zayd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no riba except in delay. No one narrated this hadith from al-Mughirah ibn Ziyad except al-Fadl ibn Musa; Zahmawayh is alone in it."
"7833","Mahmud narrated to us, Zakariyya Zahmawayh narrated to us, al-Fadl narrated to us, Aban ibn Abdillah al-Bajali narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs: that Ibn Umar did not pray before the Eid nor after it, so he was asked about it, and he said: I did not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray before it nor after it. No one narrated it from Abu Bakr except Aban, nor from Aban except al-Fadl."
"7834","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abu al-Shatha Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Sulayman, from Mujahid, from Aishah, she said: I used to make nabidh of dates for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then I would take a handful of raisins and throw it into it. No one narrated this hadith from Mujahid except Humayd ibn Sulayman, nor from Humayd except Hafs; Abu al-Shatha is alone in it."
"7835","Mahmud narrated to us, Abu al-Shatha narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Asim, from al-Shabi, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us the meat of domestic donkeys. No one narrated this hadith from al-Shabi except Asim; Hafs is alone in it."
"7836","Mahmud narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Jabir ibn al-Hurr, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed wudu three times three times. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir ibn al-Hurr except Ali ibn Hashim; Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah is alone in it."
"7837","Mahmud narrated to us, Uthman narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays, from al-Hurr ibn al-Sayyah, from Hunaydah ibn Khalid al-Khuzai, from Hafsah, she said: There are four which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never used to leave: fasting Ashura, the ten days, three days of every month, and two rakahs before the morning prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Qays except al-Ashjai, nor from al-Ashjai except Abu al-Nadr; Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah is alone in it."
"7838","Mahmud narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Hasan ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Walid, from Jami ibn Shaddad Abu Sakhrah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Alqamah al-Thaqafi, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: There were with us on the night the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept through the prayer until the sun rose, two camel-drivers. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn al-Walid except Hasan ibn Thabit; Yahya ibn Adam is alone in it."
"7839","Mahmud narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Isa ibn al-Mukhtar, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Yazid ibn al-Bara, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray four before Zuhr. This hadith is not narrated from al-Bara except with this chain; Bakr al-Qadi is alone in it."
"7840","Mahmud narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Said ibn al-Musayyab ibn Sharik narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Umar ibn Farrukh narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Zubayr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave the cupper his wage, a dinar. It is not narrated from Ibn Abbas from any source that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the cupper his wage, a dinar, except with this chain; Umar ibn Farrukh is alone in it."
"7841","Mahmud narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari narrated to us, Ismail ibn Aban al-Warraq narrated to us, Anbasah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zadham, from Umm Sad, from Aishah, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, you enter the privy and nothing of filth is seen from you? He said: Do you not know, O Aishah, that the earth swallows what comes out of the prophets, so nothing of it is seen? This hadith is not narrated from Aishah except with this chain; Ismail ibn Aban is alone in it."
"7842","Mahmud narrated to us, Abu al-Shatha Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ashath, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a woman who had stolen, so he cut off her hand, and said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if it were Fatimah the daughter of Muhammad I would have cut off her hand. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Ashath; Hafs is alone in it."
"7843","Mahmud narrated to us, Abu al-Shatha narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Wardan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer in trousers alone. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Husayn ibn Wardan; and its meaning is: that a man wraps himself in trousers alone without a shirt or a cloak."
"7844","Mahmud narrated to us, Abu al-Shatha narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Ghurab narrated to us, from Salih ibn Hayyan, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to name a dog Kalb or Kulayb. No one narrated this hadith from Salih ibn Hayyan except Ali ibn Ghurab; Abu al-Shatha is alone in it."
"7845","Mahmud narrated to us, Abu al-Shatha narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Karimah bint Sirin, she said: I accompanied Ibn Umar from Muzdalifah to Mina, and I said: I have vowed to fast Wednesday, and this day has coincided with it, what do you think? He said: Allah has commanded fulfilling vows, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting this day. No one narrated this hadith from Karimah bint Sirin, the sister of Muhammad ibn Sirin, except Asim al-Ahwal; Hafs ibn Ghiyath is alone in it."
"7846","Mahmud narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This ummah will split into seventy-three sects, all of them in the Fire except one. They said: And what is that sect? He said: Whoever is upon what I and my Companions are upon today. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except Abdullah ibn Sufyan al-Madani and Yasin al-Zayyat."
"7847","Mahmud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was granted victory by the Saba wind, and Ad were destroyed by the Dabur wind. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Abu Awanah; Muhammad ibn Aban is alone in it."
"7848","Mahmud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a donkey named Ufayr. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Yazid ibn Ata."
"7849","Mahmud narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bayan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Kufi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware the insight of the believer, for he sees with the light of Allah, then he recited: Indeed in that are signs for the discerning. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Qays except Muhammad ibn Kathir and Muhammad ibn Abi Marwan, and it is not narrated from Abu Said except with this chain."
"7850","Mahmud narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bayan narrated to us, Khalid ibn Amr al-Umawi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Suddi, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed me at his right. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Khalid ibn Amr; Abd al-Hamid ibn Bayan is alone in it, and none narrated it from al-Suddi except Sufyan."
"7851","Mahmud narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Salih ibn Umar narrated to us, from Mutarrif ibn Tarif, from Bashir ibn Muslim, from Kathir ibn Ubayd the freedman of Aishah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away between my chest and my throat. She said: And I thought that Allah would return his soul to him. She said: And likewise He does with the prophets. So he moved, and I said: If you are given a choice today you will not choose us. And it was said: That is what he said to Bilal: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer; you are like the women companions of Yusuf. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, I only said that because Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man, and if he stands in your place he will not be able to pray. No one narrated this hadith from Mutarrif except Salih ibn Amr."
"7852","Mahmud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Jarjarai narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: Prayer on a journey is two rakahs; whoever abandons the Sunnah has disbelieved. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Abdullah ibn Raja al-Makki."
"7853","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Salih, from al-Suddi, from al-Bahiyy, from Fatimah bint Qays, she said: My husband divorced me three times, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no lodging for you, nor maintenance. No one narrated this hadith from al-Suddi except al-Hasan ibn Salih; Yahya ibn Adam is alone in it."
"7854","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays al-Mulai, from Abdullah ibn Isa, from Umarah ibn Rashid, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, Abu Musa al-Ashari narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not divorce women except on suspicion of misconduct, for Allah does not love the tasting men nor the tasting women. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Qays except Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik; Wahb ibn Baqiyyah is alone in it."
"7855","Mahmud narrated to us, Wahb narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays, from Abu Ishaq, Najiyah ibn Kab narrated to us, he said: I saw Ali perform wudu, washing the face three times, the forearms three times, wiping his head, and the feet three times up to the ankles, then he took the remainder of his wudu water and drank it standing, and said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Amr ibn Qays, nor from Amr ibn Qays except Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik; Wahb ibn Baqiyyah is alone in it."
"7856","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thalabah ibn Sawa narrated to us, my uncle Muhammad ibn Sawa narrated to me, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you fights, let him avoid the face, for Allah created Adam in the image of his face. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Said; Muhammad ibn Sawa is alone in it."
"7857","Mahmud narrated to us, Bakr ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Humayd, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by children and greeted them. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Mutamir; Bakr ibn Khalaf is alone in it."
"7858","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muawiyah ibn Bakr al-Bahili narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The gifts of rulers are misappropriation. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except al-Nadr; Ahmad ibn Muawiyah is alone in it."
"7859","Mahmud narrated to us, Abu Mamar al-Qatii narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never came to me except that he prayed them, meaning: the two rakahs after Asr. No one narrated this hadith from Ammar al-Duhni except Ubaydah."
"7860","Mahmud narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Musa ibn Dinar al-Makki, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Aishah bint Sad, from Aishah the Mother of the Believers, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let Abu Bakr lead the people in prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Aishah bint Sad except Musa ibn Talhah, nor from Musa except Musa ibn Dinar; Yusuf al-Samti is alone in it."
"7861","Mahmud narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muawiyah ibn Bakr al-Bahili narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Abu al-Siddiq, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he came out of the privy would wash his seat three times. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Siddiq except Zayd al-Ammi, nor from Zayd except Jabir; Sharik is alone in it."
"7862","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Wahb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muzani narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother when it has grown hair. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ishaq except Muhammad ibn al-Hasan; Wahb ibn Baqiyyah is alone in it."
"7863","Mahmud narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muzani narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Zaynab Abu Yusuf al-Sayqali, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir ibn Abdillah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man praying who had placed his left hand over his right, so he pulled it off and placed his right hand over his left. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Sufyan except al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Zaynab, nor from al-Hajjaj except Muhammad ibn al-Hasan; Wahb ibn Baqiyyah is alone in it. And Hisham narrated it from Ibn Abi Zaynab, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Hurayrah."
"7864","Mahmud narrated to us, Abu al-Shatha Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Zuhayr, from Jabir, from Ibn Abi Nuym, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The truthful one believed, Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me: Indeed the first dispute to be judged on the Day of Resurrection: two goats, one horned and one hornless. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Nuym except Jabir, nor from Jabir except Zuhayr, nor from Zuhayr except Yahya ibn Adam; Abu al-Shatha is alone in it."
"7865","Mahmud narrated to us, Wahb narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Husayn, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity is not lawful for a rich person, nor for one of sound strength. No one narrated this hadith from Husayn except Khalid."
"7866","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu al-Shatha Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Shayban, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Abu Salih, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: al-Numan ibn Qawqal said: O Messenger of Allah, what if I pray the obligatory prayers, permit the lawful, forbid the unlawful, and add nothing to that, shall I enter Paradise? He said: Yes. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash from Abu Salih except Shayban; Ubaydullah ibn Musa is alone in it."
"7867","Mahmud narrated to us, Abu al-Shatha narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Ibrahim, from al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn: that a man freed six slaves in his illness, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them, freed two and kept four in slavery. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Ibrahim except Waki."
"7868","Mahmud narrated to us, Tamim ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Sharik, from Ismail al-Makki, from Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Abu Rafi, he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Umar ibn al-Khattab as a collector of charity, so he came to al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, and al-Abbas spoke harshly to him, so Umar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Umar, do you not know that a man's uncle is like his father; indeed al-Abbas had advanced to us his charity for the year, the year before. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman al-Ahwal except Ismail al-Makki, nor from Ismail except Sharik; Ishaq al-Azraq is alone in it."
"7869","Mahmud narrated to us, Tamim narrated to us, Ishaq narrated to us, from Sharik, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Umar ibn Abdillah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, from his father, from his grandfather Umar: that he gave a horse in charity in the time of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he saw its owner selling it at a low price, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about that, and he said: Do not buy back your charity. No one narrated this hadith from Umar ibn Abdillah ibn Umar except Hisham, nor from Hisham except Sharik; Ishaq al-Azraq is alone in it."
"7870","Mahmud narrated to us, Tamim narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from Ata, from Jabir: that a man freed a slave of his after his death, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered, and he sold him for eight hundred dirhams. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except Sharik; Ishaq al-Azraq is alone in it."
"7871","Mahmud narrated to us, Tamim narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from al-Bahiyy, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting. No one narrated this hadith from al-Suddi except Sharik and Israil; Ishaq al-Azraq is alone in it from Sharik."
"7872","Mahmud narrated to us, Tamim narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake up in a state of janabah, then complete his fast. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Sharik; Ishaq al-Azraq is alone in it."
"7873","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muzani narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail, from Ibn Abi Awfa, he said: A man put up goods for sale and swore by Allah besides Whom there is no god that he had been offered for it what he had not been offered, to entice a Muslim into it, so it was revealed: Indeed those who purchase with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab except Muhammad ibn al-Hasan; Wahb ibn Baqiyyah is alone in it."
"7874","Mahmud narrated to us, Wahb narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Awwam, from Abu Muhammad the freedman of Umar ibn al-Khattab, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sends ahead three children who have not reached puberty, they will be for him a strong fortress from the Fire. So Abu al-Darda said: I have sent ahead two, so he said: And two. So Ubayy ibn Kab, the master of the reciters, said: I have sent ahead one. He said: And one, but that is at the first shock. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ubaydah except Abu Muhammad the freedman of Umar; al-Awwam ibn Hawshab is alone in it."
"7875","Mahmud narrated to us, Wahb narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Awwam, from Udhrah ibn al-Harith, from Zuhayr, from Mahan, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that Ibn Umm Maktum came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was blind, and complained to him and asked him to grant him a concession for the Isha and Fajr prayers, and said: Between me and you there are thorny trees. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you hear the call to prayer? He said: Yes, once or twice. So he did not grant him a concession in that. No one narrated this hadith from Mahan, and he is Abu Salih, except Zuhayr, and he is Ibn al-Aqmar, from whom Amr ibn Murrah narrated, and none narrated it from Zuhayr except Udhrah ibn al-Harith; al-Awwam is alone in it."
"7876","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Isa al-Tai narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit narrated to us, Abu Harun al-Abdi narrated to us, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: Ali sent a man to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to ask him about madhiy, disliking to be the one to ask him because of Fatimah's place, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, a man sees a woman on the road and emits madhiy, is ghusl due upon him? He said: That is met by the vigor of men; wudu suffices you for that. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Harun except Muhammad ibn Thabit, and it is not narrated from Abu Said except with this chain."
"7877","Mahmud narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Ibn Masud: that he used to come every Thursday and stand without sitting, saying: Do not kill people, for among them are the elderly, the weak, and the needy. He said: So he would say: They are two; the best of guidance is the guidance of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the truest of speech is the Book of Allah, the worst of matters are the invented ones, every invention is misguidance. Beware, the wretched is he who is wretched in his mother's womb, and the fortunate is he who takes lesson from others. Beware, let not a long period pass over you, nor let hope distract you, for everything that is coming is near, and only what is not coming is far. Among the worst of people is the idler by day and the corpse by night. Killing a believer is disbelief, abusing him is wickedness, and it is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days. Beware, the worst of narrations are lying narrations, and no lying is proper, neither serious nor jesting, nor that a man promise his child then not fulfill it. Beware, lying leads to wickedness, wickedness leads to the Fire, truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise. The truthful one is called: he told the truth and did good, and the liar is called: he lied and acted wickedly. And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The servant keeps telling the truth until he is written with Allah as a truthful one, and he keeps lying until he is written with Allah as a liar. Do you know what biting slander is? It is tale-carrying and gossip; it is the backbiting that corrupts between people."
"7878","Mahmud narrated to us, Wahb narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Hammad, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the sermon of need, saying: All praise is due to Allah; we praise Him and seek His help, and we seek refuge with Allah from the evils of our souls. Whomever Allah guides none can misguide, and whomever He misguides none can guide. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone without partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Abu Ubaydah said: And I heard from Abu Musa saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Then if you wish to join your sermon with verses of the Quran, say: Fear Allah as He should be feared and do not die except as Muslims; And fear Allah through Whom you ask one another, and the wombs; indeed Allah is ever over you an Observer; Fear Allah and speak a right word; He will amend for you your deeds and forgive you your sins, and whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has certainly attained a great attainment. As for after, then speak your need."
"7879","Mahmud narrated to us, Wahb narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Ismail, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, he said: I bear witness that I heard Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said bearing witness that they heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No people ever sit remembering Allah except the angels surround them, tranquility descends upon them, mercy covers them, and Allah mentions them among those with Him. No one narrated these hadiths from Ismail ibn Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman except Khalid; Wahb ibn Baqiyyah is alone in them."
"7880","Mahmud narrated to us, Wahb narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not envy one another, do not turn away from one another, and be servants of Allah as brothers. It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days; they meet and this one turns away and this one turns away, and the one who begins with greeting precedes to Paradise. None of those who narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri said: and the one who begins with greeting precedes to Paradise, except Abdullah ibn Umar, nor from Abdullah ibn Umar except Khalid; Wahb ibn Baqiyyah is alone in it. And Abu Nuaym narrated it from Abdullah ibn Umar."
"7881","Mahmud narrated to us, Wahb narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from al-Fadl Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Said ibn Abi Sadaqah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Imran. I said: At your service. He said: Say: O Allah, I ask You for guidance to what is right in my affair, and I seek refuge with You from the evil of my soul. No one narrated this hadith from Said ibn Abi Sadaqah except al-Fadl Abu Abd al-Rahman, nor from al-Fadl except Khalid; Wahb ibn Baqiyyah is alone in it."
"7882","Mahmud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Jarjarai narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Nafi, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the hadith of the cave. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Nafi except Jarir; Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah is alone in it."
"7883","Mahmud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Jarjarai narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I remember from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr and Umar, that when they said takbir they recited: All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Muhammad ibn Fudayl; Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah is alone in it."
"7884","Mahmud narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn Abdillah ibn Umar, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) consulted the Muslims about what would gather them for prayer, so they said: the horn, but he disliked it because of the Jews, then they mentioned the bell, but he disliked it because of the Christians, then on that night a man of the Ansar called Abdullah ibn Zayd, and Umar ibn al-Khattab, were shown the call to prayer. So the Ansari knocked on the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night, so the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Bilal, and he called the adhan with it. So Umar said: Indeed I saw the like of what he saw, but he preceded me. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, nor from Abd al-Rahman except Khalid."
"7885","Mahmud narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever meets Allah associating nothing with Him enters Paradise, and whoever meets Him associating anything with Him enters the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman except Khalid."
"7886","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Zayd ibn Abi al-Attab, from Amr ibn Sulaym, from Abu Qatadah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying with the daughter of Abu al-As, carrying her when he stood and putting her down when he sat, until he finished his prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Abi al-Attab except Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq."
"7887","Mahmud narrated to us, Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Ishaq ibn Abdillah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the shepherds to stone the jamarat at night. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Ishaq ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Farwah, nor from Ishaq except Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq; Khalid is alone in it."
"7888","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, that a woman lifted up to him a son of hers in a cloth and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there Hajj for this one? He said: Yes, and for you is a reward. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq except Khalid."
"7889","Mahmud narrated to us, Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah has the like of his reward, and whoever looks after a warrior's family with good, or spends on his family, has the like of his reward. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Zayd except Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq."
"7890","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali, from his father, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate, saying: O Allah, let me enjoy my hearing and my sight until You make them surviving from me, grant me health in my religion, gather me upon what You have kept me alive, help me against whoever wrongs me until You show me my vengeance from him. O Allah, I have submitted my religion to You, turned my face to You, entrusted my affair to You, and laid my back upon You; there is no refuge nor escape from You except to You. I believe in Your messengers whom You sent, and in Your Book which You revealed. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Uqbah except Abdullah ibn Jafar; Dawud ibn Rushayd is alone in it."
"7891","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Sahl ibn al-Abbas al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, Said ibn Salim al-Qaddah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with three rakahs, making the qunut before bowing. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Said ibn Salim."
"7892","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Jamil ibn Yazid al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Musayyab ibn Sharik narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Zayyat, from Yusuf ibn Suhayb, from Habib ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who does not trim his mustache. No one narrated this hadith from Hamzah al-Zayyat except al-Musayyab ibn Sharik; Jamil ibn Yazid is alone in it."
"7893","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Ibrahim al-Ansari al-Balkhi narrated to us, Asram ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from Qurrah ibn Khalid, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Today is training, tomorrow is the race, and the goal is Paradise or the Fire. I am the first, Abu Bakr the second, Umar the third, and the people after are by precedence, the first then the first. No one narrated this hadith from Qurrah except Asram ibn Hawshab."
"7894","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Hamid ibn Adam al-Marwazi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Shinzhir, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought two disputants, and said: Judge between them, O Uqbah. I said: Should I judge while you are present? He said: Judge between them. I said: On what basis? He said: If you strive and are right, for you are two good deeds, and if you err, for you is one good deed. No one narrated this hadith from Kathir ibn Shinzhir except Hafs ibn Sulayman; Hamid ibn Adam is alone in it."
"7895","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ali ibn Hujr al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muhammad al-Muwaqqari narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to me and saw a piece of bread thrown aside, so he walked to it, wiped it, and said: O Aishah, treat the blessings of Allah well, for they rarely flee from a household and almost return to them. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except al-Muwaqqari."
"7896","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped after he said: The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Qilabah except Abu Sufyan, and he is al-Sadi, his name is Tarif; Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari is alone in it."
"7897","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Sahl ibn al-Abbas al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn al-Wazir al-Sadi al-Kufi narrated to us, from Abu Janab al-Kalbi, from Kinanah al-Adawi, from Abu al-Darda, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says when he goes to his bed: Praise be to Allah Who is High and irresistible, hidden and aware, sovereign and decreeing; praise be to Allah Who gives life and death, and He is over all things capable, emerges from his sins as on the day his mother bore him. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Janab except Ishaq ibn al-Wazir; Sahl ibn al-Abbas is alone in it."
"7898","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Hamid ibn Adam narrated to us, Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, and from Habib al-Muallim, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray barefoot and shod. And I saw him drink standing and sitting. And I saw him turn from prayer to his right and to his left. And I saw him fast on journeys and break fast. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Said, nor from Said except Abdah; Hamid ibn Adam is alone in it."
"7899","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Hamid ibn Adam narrated to us, Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam is ten shares, and he who has no share has failed: bearing witness that there is no god but Allah, and it is the religion; the second is prayer, and it is the natural disposition; the third is zakat, and it is purification; the fourth is fasting, and it is a shield; the fifth is Hajj, and it is the law; the sixth is jihad, and it is the handhold; the seventh is enjoining good, and it is fulfillment; the eighth is forbidding evil, and it is the proof; the ninth is the community, and it is unity; the tenth is obedience, and it is protection. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid al-Hadhdha except Ali ibn Asim; Hamid ibn Adam is alone in it."
"7900","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Hamid ibn Adam narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between his Companions, between the Emigrants and the Helpers, he did not make brotherhood between Ali ibn Abi Talib and any of them. So Ali went out angry until he came to a stream of land and pillowed his arm, and the wind blew dust upon him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought him until he found him, nudged him with his foot, and said to him: Get up, you are fit to be only Abu Turab. Are you angry with me because I made brotherhood between the Emigrants and Helpers and did not make brotherhood between you and any of them? Are you not pleased to be from me in the position of Harun from Musa, except that there is no prophet after me? Beware, whoever loves you is surrounded by security and faith, and whoever hates you, Allah will cause him to die the death of ignorance, and he will be reckoned for his deeds in Islam. No one narrated this hadith from Mujahid except Layth, nor from Layth except Jarir; Hamid ibn Adam is alone in it."
"7901","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Hamid ibn Adam narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good deeds are multiplied on Friday. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except al-Fadl ibn Musa."
"7902","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Khidr ibn Akhram al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Jarud ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The soul gets bored, and none of you knows the extent of the period, so let him look at what worship he can bear, then persist in it, for the most beloved deeds to Allah are those persisted in even if little. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ishaq except al-Jarud ibn Yazid; Ibn Ishaq is alone in it."
"7903","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Khidr ibn Adam al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Jarud ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ziyad ibn Saman, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: I walked with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to a woman of the Ansar, so she spread for him a mat of palm leaves and slaughtered a sheep for him. While we were thus, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come to you a man of the people of Paradise. Then Abu Bakr al-Siddiq came. Then he said: There will come to you a man of the people of Paradise. Then Umar ibn al-Khattab came. Then he said: There will come to you a man of the people of Paradise; O Allah, if You will, make him Ali. Then Ali ibn Abi Talib came. Then food was brought to us and we ate, then we stood and prayed Zuhr without performing wudu, then we returned to the rest of our food and ate, and neither the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) renewed wudu nor any of us. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except Ibn Saman; al-Jarud ibn Yazid is alone in it."
"7904","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Khidr narrated to us, al-Jarud narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not for a Muslim to humiliate himself. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how does he humiliate himself? He said: He exposes himself to a trial he cannot bear. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Israil; al-Jarud is alone in it, and it is not narrated from Ali except with this chain."
"7905","Mahmud narrated to us, al-Khidr narrated to us, al-Jarud narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that dogs are a community among communities, I would have ordered killing them; so kill from them every jet-black one, and whoever keeps a dog for other than hunting, crops, or sheep, there comes to him every night a qirat of sin like Uhud. And when a dog laps in the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times, one of them with dust. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except al-Jarud, and it is not narrated from Ali except with this chain."
"7906","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ali ibn Hujr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no marriage except with a guardian. No one narrated this hadith from Sharik except Ali ibn Hujr."
"7907","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: Allah made prayer obligatory as two rakahs, then increased it in residence and left it as is on journeys. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ajlan except Ibn al-Mubarak."
"7908","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Irak ibn Malik, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in Makkah in the year of the conquest fifteen days shortening prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah except Irak ibn Malik, nor from Irak except Yazid, nor from Yazid except Ibn Luhayah; Ibn al-Mubarak is alone in it."
"7909","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Sahl ibn al-Abbas al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays behind an imam, the recitation of the imam is recitation for him. No one raised this hadith among those who narrated it from Ibn Ulayyah except Sahl ibn al-Abbas, and others narrated it as stopped."
"7910","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs ibn Ibrahim al-Ansari al-Balkhi narrated to us, Amr ibn Harun narrated to us, from al-Mubarak ibn Fadalah, from Abu Harun, from Abu Said al-Khudri: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey in Ramadan and broke fast with Ajwah dates. No one narrated this hadith from Mubarak ibn Fadalah except Amr ibn Harun."
"7911","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ali ibn Hujr narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muhammad al-Muwaqqari narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pass by boys, greet them, and supplicate for blessing for them. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except al-Muwaqqari."
"7912","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Hamid ibn Adam al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah al-Arzami, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Jundub ibn Sufyan al-Bajali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant conceals a secret but Allah clothes him with its garment; if good then good, and if evil then evil. No one narrated this hadith from Salamah ibn Kuhayl except al-Arzami."
"7913","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Abbas al-Bahili narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Atiyyah al-Saffar narrated to us, Matar al-Warraq narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to take fresh dates in his right hand and watermelon in his left, eating fresh dates with watermelon, and it was the most beloved fruit to him. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Matar; Yusuf ibn Atiyyah is alone in it."
"7914","Mahmud ibn al-Faraj al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Ammar will be killed by the rebellious party. So Muawiyah said: You keep dredging your urine; did we kill him? Those who brought him out killed him. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Ismail ibn Amr."
"7915","Mahmud ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr narrated to us, Hammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing Umrah, so his Companions exited ihram, but I had menstruated and was not pure until I arrived at Makkah, and Arafah came and I was not pure. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Undo your hair and bathe, then perform Hajj until when it was the night of departure, he said to Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr: Take her out of the sanctuary, then make her perform Umrah. No one narrated this hadith from Habib except Hammad ibn Shuayb."
"7916","Mahmud ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr narrated to us, Hammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The people of polytheism used to chant the talbiyah: At Your service, O Allah, at Your service; at Your service, no partner have You, except a partner that is Yours; You own him and what he owns. So Allah revealed: Do you have among what your right hands possess any partners in what We have provided you, so you are equal therein, fearing them as you fear yourselves. No one narrated this hadith from Habib except Hammad ibn Shuayb."
"7917","Mahmud ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr narrated to us, Sharik and Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved deeds to Allah after the obligations is bringing joy to a Muslim. No one narrated this hadith from Layth except Sharik and Jarir; Ismail ibn Amr is alone in it."
"7918","Mahmud ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever satisfies his appetite in this world will be separated from his desire in the Hereafter; whoever stretches his eye to the adornment of the luxurious will be abased in the kingdom of this world; and whoever bears severe hardship with beautiful patience, Allah will settle him in Firdaws wherever he wills. No one narrated this hadith from Adi ibn Thabit except Fudayl ibn Marzuq; Ismail ibn Amr is alone in it, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"7919","Mahmud narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fada narrated to us, from his father, from Alqamah ibn Abdillah al-Muzani, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you are in reeds, mud, or snow, and prayer comes, gesture with gestures. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Fada except Ismail and Madi ibn Sinan."
"7920","Mahmud ibn Ali al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya Saiqah narrated to us, Ali ibn Thabit al-Dahhan narrated to us, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Amr ibn Hafs, from Sad, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: What a good death is a man's death defending his right. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir except Asbat ibn Nasr; Ali ibn Thabit is alone in it."
"7921","Mahmud ibn Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, he said: My father had left praying with us. I said: Why have you left praying with us? He said: You shorten. I said: Then where is the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): For among you are the weak, the elderly, and the needy? He said: I heard Abdullah ibn Masud say that, then he prayed three times what you pray. No one narrated this hadith from Ammar except Abd al-Jabbar; Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri is alone in it."
"7922","Mahmud narrated to us, Abu Yahya narrated to us, Shabbabah ibn Sawwar narrated to us, Yusuf ibn al-Khattab al-Madani narrated to us, from Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three traits are in a hypocrite: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks, and when entrusted he betrays. This hadith is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain; Shabbabah is alone in it."
"7923","Mahmud narrated to us, Abu Yahya narrated to us, Ali ibn Qadim narrated to us, Jafar ibn Ziyad al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Ali, he said: I suffered a pain, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he seated me in his place, stood praying, threw the edge of his garment over me, then said: You are cured, O son of Abu Talib; no harm upon you. I have not asked Allah for anything but I asked the like of it for you, and I have not asked Allah for anything but He gave it to me, except that it was said to me: There is no prophet after you. No one narrated this hadith from Jafar al-Ahmar except Ali ibn Qadim."
"7924","Mahmud ibn Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya narrated to us, Ismail ibn Umar Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, from Wail ibn Dawud, from Abayah ibn Rifah, from Rafi ibn Khadij, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which earnings are purest? He said: A man's work with his hand, and every blessed sale. No one narrated this hadith from Wail ibn Dawud except al-Masudi."
"7925","Mahmud narrated to us, Harun ibn Musa al-Farawi narrated to us, Abu Damrah Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said said: Amr ibn Shuayb narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is disbelief for a man to claim a lineage he does not know, and to deny it even if slight. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except Abu Damrah."
"7926","Mahmud narrated to us, Harun ibn Musa narrated to us, Sad ibn Said al-Maqburi narrated to us, from his brother, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: I bear witness upon my beloved (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that I heard him say: Allah will shade in the shade of His Throne on the Day of Resurrection whoever grants respite to one in difficulty, or helps one lacking skill. No one narrated this hadith from Said al-Maqburi except his son."
"7927","Mahmud ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Salamah Yahya ibn al-Mughirah al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Ibn Rafi narrated to me, from Uthman ibn al-Dahhak, from his father, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to shorten prayer at al-Aqiq. No one narrated this hadith as raised from Nafi except al-Dahhak; his son is alone in it."
"7928","Mahmud narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Ibn Nafi narrated to us, from al-Layth ibn Sad, from Bakr ibn Sawadah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: Two men went out on a journey, prayer came upon them and they had no water, so they made tayammum with clean earth and prayed. Then they found water afterwards within the time, so one of them repeated and the other did not repeat. Then they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. So he said to the one who did not repeat: You hit the Sunnah, and your prayer sufficed you. And he said to the one who performed wudu and repeated: For you is the reward twice. No one narrated this hadith well-formed from al-Layth ibn Sad except Abdullah ibn Nafi."
"7929","Mahmud ibn Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Ibn Nafi narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq never sat in the seat of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the pulpit until he met Allah; Umar never sat in Abu Bakr's seat until he met Allah; and Uthman never sat in Umar's seat until he met Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Abdullah ibn Umar."
"7930","And with it Ibn Nafi narrated to me, from Asim ibn Umar, from Humayd ibn Qays, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered killing snakes in ihram and in the sanctuary. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Humayd ibn Qays, nor from Humayd except Asim ibn Umar; Ibn Nafi is alone in it."
"7931","And with it Ibn Nafi narrated to me, from Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, it will be called: Where are the children of sixty, and it is the age about which Allah the Exalted said: Did We not give you life long enough to remember, whoever would remember, and the warner came to you. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn, nor from Ibn Abi Husayn except Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl; Ibn Nafi is alone in it."
"7932","And with it Ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Abu al-Malih, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees in his brother a defect in religion and conceals it, it will be a good deed for him on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Malih al-Madani from Abu Salih, and he is al-Khuziyy, except Ibn Nafi and Marwan ibn Muawiyah."
"7933","And with it Ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Asim ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever is rain-watered or from springs, in every ten is one."
"7934","And with it Ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Asim ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he gave his wives a choice, the one who chose herself was a woman of Banu Hilal."
"7935","And with it, from Asim ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel a journey of three nights except with a mahram of hers."
"7936","And with it, from Asim ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he performed Hajj with his wives, said: This is only this once, then you must stay upon the backs of mats."
"7937","And with it, from Asim ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell."
"7938","And with it: from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever is cut from a beast while it is alive, what is cut of its flesh, let no one eat it."
"7939","And with it: from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came to Makkah, found there three hundred and sixty idols, so he pointed with his staff at each idol and said: Truth has come and falsehood has perished; indeed falsehood is ever perishing, and the idol fell without him touching it."
"7940","And with it: from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is forbidden, and every intoxicant is wine."
"7941","And with it: from Ibn Umar, he said: The truce between the Prophet and the people of Makkah at al-Hudaybiyah was four years."
"7942","And with it: from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raced horses, placed a prize between them, placed among them a trailing horse, and said: There is no prize except in hoof, or arrowhead."
"7943","Mahmud ibn Ali narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Salimi narrated to us, Ibn Nafi narrated to me, from Asim ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reserved al-Naqi for the horses of the Muslims."
"7944","And with it: from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is invited to a wedding feast and does not come to it has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"7945","And with it: from Ibn Umar: that a woman was found killed in one of the expeditions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) denounced that and forbade killing women and children."
"7946","Mahmud ibn Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Mughirah al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Ibn Nafi narrated to me, from Asim ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, that Salim ibn Abdillah ibn Umar informed him, that Abdullah ibn Umar informed him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told while at al-Muarras, meaning the resting place of the tree: You are in a blessed valley. No one narrated these hadiths from Asim ibn Umar except Abdullah ibn Nafi al-Saigh."
"7947","Mahmud ibn Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Mughirah al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling wala or gifting it. None narrates this hadith from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman except Ibn Abi Fudayk."
"7948","And with it, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Abu al-Zinad, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for his ihram when he entered ihram, and for his release before he performed tawaf, with the best I found. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zinad except al-Dahhak ibn Uthman; Ibn Abi Fudayk is alone in it."
"7949","Mahmud ibn Ali narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Salimi narrated to us, Ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Bilal ibn Abi Bakr, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is wine, and every wine is forbidden; its little and its much are alike."
"7950","Mahmud ibn Ali narrated to us, Ahmad narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farawi narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded cupping and said: People have not drawn anything better than it, or a drink of honey. This hadith is not narrated from al-Saib ibn Yazid except with this chain; Ishaq al-Farawi is alone in it."
"7951","And with it Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Abu Musa al-Khayyat, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you performs wudu, let him rinse his mouth three times, for sins come out of his face, wash his hands, wipe his head three times, then insert his hands into his ears, then pour over his feet three times. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Abu Musa, whose name is Isa ibn Abi Isa; Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik is alone in it."
"7952","Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The two farthest men of the Ansar in dwelling from the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were Abu Lubabah ibn Abd al-Mundhir, his family at Quba, and Abu Abs ibn Jubayr, his dwelling among Banu Harithah; they would pray Asr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then come to their people, who had not yet prayed, due to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastening the Asr prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah except Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"7953","Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from al-Wadin ibn Ata, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Uqbah ibn Amir, he said: I came with twelve riders until we alighted at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). My companions said: Who will graze our camels while we go to learn from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he rests we will pass on to him what we heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I said: I will. Then I said to myself: Perhaps I am cheated; my companions hear what I do not hear from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I attended one day and heard a man say: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs a complete wudu, then stands for his prayer, is free of his sin as on the day his mother bore him. I was amazed at that, so Umar ibn al-Khattab said: How would you be if you heard the other speech? You would be more amazed. I said: Repeat to me, may Allah make me your ransom. So Umar ibn al-Khattab said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies not associating anything with Allah the Exalted, the gates of Paradise are opened for him; he enters through whichever he wills, and it has eight gates. Then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us, so I sat facing him, and he turned his face away from me. So I stood and faced him, and he did that three times. When it was the fourth, I said: O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be for you, why do you turn your face away from me? So he turned to me and said: Is one dearer to you or twelve? Twice or thrice. When I saw that, I returned to my companions. No one narrated this hadith from al-Wadin ibn Ata except Yahya ibn Hamzah."
"7954","Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, Nasr ibn Alqamah narrated to me, from Umayr ibn al-Aswad and Kathir ibn Murrah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will always be a group of my ummah standing upon the command of Allah; those who oppose them do not harm them, fighting their enemies. Whenever one war ends, the war of other people begins; Allah raises a people and provides them from it until the Hour comes to them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are the people of Sham. No one narrated this hadith from Nasr ibn Alqamah except Yahya ibn Hamzah."
"7955","Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Salih, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to place the vessel for her, so she would drink, then he would perform wudu with her remainder, meaning: the cat. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Salih except al-Darawardi."
"7956","Musa ibn Isa narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Abu Dharr: that he used to serve the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he finished his service he would come to the mosque and lie down in it. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Dharr except with this chain; Ismail ibn Ayyash is alone in it."
"7957","Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated to us, Amr ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, he said: We visited Yazid ibn al-Aswad when sick, then Wathilah ibn al-Asqa came in to him. When he saw him, he stretched his hand, took his hand, and wiped his face and chest with it, because he had pledged with it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said to him: O Yazid, what is your opinion of your Lord? He said: Good. He said: Then rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah the Exalted says: I am with My servant's opinion of Me; if good then good, and if evil then evil. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus ibn Maysarah except Amr ibn Waqid."
"7958","Musa ibn Isa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Amr ibn Waqid narrated to us, Zura ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I give you private nabidh or public nabidh? He said: Rather public nabidh. No one narrated this hadith from Zura ibn Ibrahim except Amr ibn Waqid; Muhammad ibn Mubarak is alone in it."
"7959","Musa ibn Isa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Amr ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah brighten a servant who hears this speech of mine and does not add to it; how many a bearer of a word to one more comprehending of it than him. Three over which the heart of a believer does not harbor deceit: sincerity of deed for Allah, sincere advice to the rulers, and holding to the community of the Muslims, for their supplication surrounds those behind them. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus ibn Maysarah except Amr ibn Waqid, and it is not narrated from Muadh except with this chain."
"7960","Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Amr ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu al-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Beware, asceticism in this world is not by forbidding the lawful nor wasting wealth; but asceticism in this world is that you are not more confident in what is in your hands than in what is in Allah's Hands, and that you are more desirous of the reward of a calamity when afflicted by it than if it had remained for you. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Amr ibn Waqid, and it is not narrated from Abu al-Darda except with this chain."
"7961","Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Amr ibn Waqid narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Idris, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: On the Day of Resurrection will be brought one deprived of reason, one who perished in the interval, and one who perished young. The one deprived of reason will say: O Lord, had You given me reason, none given reason would be happier with his reason than me. The one who perished in the interval will say: O Lord, had a covenant from You come to me, none to whom a covenant came would be happier with his covenant than me. The young perished one will say: Had You given me a lifespan, none given a lifespan would be happier with his lifespan than me. So the Lord, blessed and exalted, will say: I command you with a matter, will you obey Me? They will say: Yes, by Your might. He will say: Go and enter the Fire. Had they entered it, it would not have harmed them. He said: Then grasping flames will come out upon them, and they will think they have destroyed everything Allah created. So they will return quickly. He said: They will say: We came out, O Lord, by Your might, wanting to enter it, but grasping flames came out upon us, and we thought they had destroyed everything Allah created. So He will command them a second time, and they will return likewise, saying like their saying. So Allah, blessed and exalted, will say: Before you were created I knew what you would do, upon My knowledge I created you, and to My knowledge you return. So the Fire will seize them. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus ibn Maysarah except Amr ibn Waqid, and it is not narrated from Muadh except with this chain."
"7962","Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Amr ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Maysarah, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me a deed which if I do it I will enter Paradise. He said: Do not associate anything with Allah, even if you are tortured and burned. Obey your parents, even if they remove you from your wealth and from everything that is yours. Do not abandon prayer deliberately, for whoever abandons prayer deliberately, the protection of Allah is free of him. Do not drink wine, for it is the key to every evil. Do not dispute authority with its people, even if you see that it is yours. Spend from your means upon your family, do not lift your stick from them, and make them fear Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Amr ibn Waqid, and it is not narrated from Muadh except with this chain."
"7963","And with it, from Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, he said: I heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan upon the pulpit say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whomever Allah wills good for, He gives him understanding in religion."
"7964","He said: And the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us one day and said: Do they say that I am the last of you to die? We said: Yes. He said: No, I am the first of you to die, then you will come in groups, some of you following others."
"7965","He said: And I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will always be a group of my ummah standing upon the truth, not caring who opposes them and who forsakes them, until the command of Allah comes while they are dominant over people. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus ibn Maysarah except Amr ibn Waqid."
"7966","Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr al-Hadrami, he said: Aishah said: The last food the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate was food containing onion. This hadith is not narrated from Aishah except with this chain; Bahir ibn Sad is alone in it."
"7967","Musa ibn Isa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Ayyub, from Shurahbil ibn Sharik, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not care what I do, nor what I commit, when I drink theriac, hang an amulet, or utter poetry from myself. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As except with this chain; Muawiyah ibn Yahya is alone in it."
"7968","Musa ibn Isa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Damdam ibn Zurah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib and Abu Umamah, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the ruler seeks suspicion among the subjects, he corrupts them. No one narrated this hadith from Damdam ibn Zurah except Ismail ibn Ayyash, and it is not narrated from al-Miqdam and Abu Umamah except with this chain."
"7969","Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb al-Abrash narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not righteousness. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Muhammad ibn Harb."
"7970","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar al-Khattabi narrated to us, Maslamah ibn Alqamah narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Three things I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Banu Tamim; I will never hate Banu Tamim after them ever. Aishah vowed to free a freedman from the children of Ismail, so captives of Banu al-Anbar were brought, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: If it pleases you to free from the children of Ismail, free from these. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made them of the children of Ismail. And cattle from the charity livestock of Sad were brought; when its beauty startled him he said: This is the charity of my people. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called them his people, and said: They are the fiercest of people in fighting in the great battles. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except Maslamah."
"7971","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are but like a hundred camels; you can hardly find among them a riding camel. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except al-Darawardi."
"7972","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are like a hundred camels; no riding camel is found among them. No one narrated this hadith from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah except Wuhayb. And Abd al-Razzaq narrated it from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father."
"7973","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muawiyah al-Jumahi narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Husayn al-Sadusi narrated to us, my uncle, whose name is Ziyad, narrated to us, from my grandfather, he said: We came to Madinah while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in it, and I had camels with me. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, order the people of the outskirts to treat me well and help me. So they stood with me. When I sold my camels, I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to me: Come near. So he wiped over my forelock and supplicated for me three times. No one narrated this hadith from Nuaym ibn Husayn except Abdullah ibn Muawiyah, and he is Nuaym ibn so-and-so ibn Husayn, and his grandfather is Husayn al-Sadusi."
"7974","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ata ibn Khalid ibn al-Zubayr ibn Abdillah ibn Rudayh ibn Dhuayb al-Anbari narrated to us, my father Khalid narrated to us, from his father al-Zubayr, from his father Abdillah, from his father Rudayh, from his father Dhuayb, that the delegation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Umm Zubayb and took her water-skin bag. So Zubayb caught up with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, the delegation took my mother's bag. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return to him his mother's bag. So he took from the one who took his mother's bag a sa of barley, his sword, and his belt. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hand, wiped with it the head of Zubayb, then said: May Allah bless you, O boy, and bless your mother through you."
"7975","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ata ibn Khalid narrated to us, my father Khalid narrated to me, from his father al-Zubayr, from his father Abdillah, from his father Rudayh, from his father Dhuayb, that Aishah said: O Prophet of Allah, I want a freed slave from the children of Ismail specifically. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Wait until the tribute of al-Anbar comes tomorrow. So the tribute of al-Anbar came, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Take from them four boys, bright and handsome, whose heads are not hidden among them. Ata ibn Khalid said: So she took my grandfather Rudayh, my cousin Samurah, my cousin's son Rukhayya, and my uncle Zubayb. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hand, wiped their heads with it, blessed them, then said: These, O Aishah, are specifically from the children of Ismail. These two hadiths are not narrated from Dhuayb al-Anbari except with this chain; Ata ibn Khalid is alone in them."
"7976","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Ammar al-Duhni narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: My uncle Jadd ibn Qays invited me among seventy riders who took upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the Ansar. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us with his uncle al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, and he said: O uncle, take upon your maternal uncles. The seventy said to him: O Muhammad, ask for your Lord and for yourself whatever you wish. He said: As for what I ask for my Lord, that you worship Him and do not associate anything with Him, and as for what I ask you for myself, that you protect me as you protect yourselves. They said: What is for us if we do that? He said: Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Ammar al-Duhni except his son Muawiyah; Muhammad ibn Imran alone narrated it."
"7977","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The banner of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was black. No one narrated this hadith from Ammar except Sharik; Muhammad ibn Imran alone narrated it."
"7978","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Nuh ibn Habib al-Qumasi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah narrated to us, he said: I heard Said ibn al-Musayyib saying: I heard Sad saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined for me both his parents on the day of Uhud. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Harmalah except Yahya ibn Said; Nuh ibn Habib alone narrated it."
"7979","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Hannat narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj and Uthman ibn al-Aswad, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If people were given according to their claims, men would claim the wealth and blood of people. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman ibn al-Aswad except Ibn Idris; al-Hasan ibn Sahl alone narrated it."
"7980","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Zarrad al-Qumasi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one has the right to prevent his neighbor from placing wood upon his wall. No one narrated this hadith from Sad ibn Ibrahim except Ibn Abi Dhib, nor from Ibn Abi Dhib except Ibn Abi Fudayk; Ibrahim ibn Ishaq alone narrated it."
"7981","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Waki narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to examine the eye and the ear. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, except Abu Waki; Muhammad ibn Bakkar alone narrated it. And the people narrated it: from Abu Ishaq, from Shurayh ibn al-Numan."
"7982","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Said, except Mamar; Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad alone narrated it."
"7983","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz informed us, from Qurrah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani, from Amr ibn al-As and Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah has added for you a prayer better for you than red camels: al-Witr, and it is for you between the Isha prayer until the rising of dawn. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Abi Habib except Qurrah ibn Abd al-Rahman; Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz alone narrated it, and it was not narrated from Amr ibn al-As and Uqbah ibn Amir except with this chain."
"7984","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Harithi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Ghasil narrated to us, from Usayd ibn Ali, from his father Ali ibn Ubayd, from Abu Usayd who said: While I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man from the Ansar came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, has anything remained upon me of kindness to my parents after their death by which I may be kind to them? He said: Yes, four qualities: praying upon them, seeking forgiveness for them, fulfilling their covenant after their death, honoring their friend, and joining the kinship by which you have no kin except through them."
"7985","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahib narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abd al-Karim, from Abdullah ibn al-Tayyib, from Umm Salamah bint Abi Hakim, who said: I reached the elderly women while they were praying the obligatory prayers with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith is not narrated from Umm Salamah bint Abi Hakim except with this chain."
"7986","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ubayd ibn Abi Karimah al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ibn Ulathah, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when he sent me to Thaqif: Be brief in prayer, O Uthman, and lead the people with the weakest of them, for among them is the weak, the one in need, the pregnant, and the nursing, and I hear the crying of the boy and so I am brief. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Ibn Ulathah; Muhammad ibn Salamah alone narrated it."
"7987","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Muhammad al-Hanafi narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated to us, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not one whose neighbor is not safe from his harms. No one narrated this hadith from Qays ibn Talq except Ayyub ibn Utbah; Hammad ibn Muhammad alone narrated it."
"7988","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Karabisi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Thabit of Banu Abd al-Awwal narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Musab of Banu Abd al-Dar narrated to me, from Muharrar ibn Abi Hurayrah, from his father who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not sleep a night nor wake except that he cleaned his teeth with the siwak. No one narrated this hadith from Muharrar ibn Abi Hurayrah except Ikrimah ibn Musab, nor from Ikrimah except Ibrahim ibn Thabit; Said ibn Abd al-Jabbar alone narrated it."
"7989","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Said ibn Zunbur narrated to us, Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he married Fatimah, said: O Ali, do not enter upon your wife until you present something. He said: I have nothing, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Give her your Hutamiyyah armor. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Mamar, nor from Mamar except Abd al-Majid; Said ibn Zunbur alone narrated it."
"7990","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, Asim ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ashjai narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhubab, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: One who declares the lawful unlawful is like one who declares the unlawful lawful."
"7991","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Aruzzi narrated to us, Abu Tumaylah Yahya ibn Wadih narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Ziyad, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The prayer time came while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when a cup of water was brought, so we performed ablution from it, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took with his hand, then placed his palm upon its mouth, then said: Pour the ablution, so we performed ablution from it, and water came out to us from the cup from between his fingers until we finished. I said to him: How many were the people, O Abu Hamzah? He said: Two hundred men. And Humayd al-Tawil also narrated to me, he said: They were eighty men."
"7992","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ismail ibn Musa al-Suddi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ayyash ibn al-Maafiri, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Ibn Abbas who said: When the prohibition of wine came down, they said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we sell it? He said: The One who forbade drinking it forbade its price; pour it out. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyash al-Maafiri except Sharik."
"7993","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, I do not know it except from Anas, raising it, he said: Allah, blessed and exalted, said: I do not take away the chosen one of My servant and then accept for him a reward less than Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except Muhammad ibn Mutarrif, nor from Muhammad ibn Mutarrif except Yazid ibn Harun; Ishaq ibn Rahawayh alone narrated it."
"7994","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Saffar narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Said narrated to us, from Kamil Abu al-Ala, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he used to recite on Friday in Fajr, Alif Lam Mim Tanzil and Hal Ata. No one narrated this hadith from Kamil except Ubayd ibn Said."
"7995","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Sahl ibn Salih al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: I saw Yazid ibn Abi Mansur, and he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: When we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and a tree separated us, then when we met, some of us would greet others. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain."
"7996","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ayyub, the companion of al-Basri, narrated to us, Harun ibn Dinar narrated to us, from his father who said: I heard a man from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), called Maymun ibn Sinbadh, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The support of my ummah is by its wicked ones. This hadith is not narrated from Maymun except with this chain; Harun ibn Dinar alone narrated it."
"7997","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Muammal, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I were invited to a shank I would answer. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Mulaykah except Abdullah ibn al-Muammal; Bishr ibn al-Sari alone narrated it."
"7998","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Husayn al-Qantari narrated to us, Mubashshir ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas who said: Whoever hears Hayya ala al-falah and does not answer, he has abandoned the sunnah of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Maymun ibn Mihran except Jafar ibn Burqan, nor from Jafar except Mubashshir; al-Abbas ibn al-Husayn alone narrated it."
"7999","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Sini narrated to us, Yaqub al-Qummi narrated to us, from Isa ibn Jariyah al-Ansari, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed at Mina five prayers: Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, the last Isha, and Fajr. No one narrated this hadith from Yaqub al-Qummi except Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Sini."
"8000","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahib al-Harithi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rakahs after Friday. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahib."
"8001","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar al-Khattabi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that Umar said: May Allah fight so-and-so, he sells wine; he heard the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): May Allah curse the Jews, fats were forbidden for them to eat, then they sold them. No one narrated this hadith from Rawh, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, except Yazid ibn Zuray; Abdullah ibn Umar al-Khattabi alone narrated it."
"8002","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahib al-Harithi narrated to us, Abu Shihab al-Hannat narrated to us, from Awf, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined between Zuhr and Asr, and between Maghrib and Isha, and delayed Maghrib and hastened Isha and prayed them together. No one narrated this hadith from Awf except Abu Shihab; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahib alone narrated it."
"8003","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Yazid ibn Maymun ibn Mihran narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim said: Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would see semen in his garment, then scratch it off and pray in it. No one narrated this hadith from Ikrimah ibn Ammar, from al-Qasim, except Yazid ibn Abdullah."
"8004","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Nafi al-Abdi in Aleppo informed me, he said: My father said to me: al-Mundhir ibn Sawa came as a delegation from Bahrain until he came to the city of the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with al-Mundhir were people, and I was a young boy who did not understand, holding their camels. He said: They went with their weapons, and greeted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and al-Mundhir put down his weapon, wore clothes he had with him, and wiped his beard with oil, then came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted, while I was with the camels looking at the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Mundhir said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: I saw in you what I did not see in your companions. I said: What did you see in me, O Prophet of Allah? He said: You put down your weapon, wore your clothes, and oiled yourself. I said: O Prophet of Allah, is it something I was naturally given or something I newly did? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: No, rather something you were naturally given. They greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Abd al-Qays accepted Islam willingly, and the people accepted Islam unwillingly, so may Allah bless Abd al-Qays and the freedmen of Abd al-Qays. My father said to me: I looked at the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as I look at you, but I did not understand. He said: And my father died when he was one hundred and twenty years old. This hadith is not narrated from Nafi al-Abdi except with this chain; Ishaq ibn Rahawayh alone narrated it."
"8005","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, my uncle al-Wasim ibn Jamil narrated to me, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Murri, from his father, that a man came to Ibn Umar and asked him, so he threw to him his turban, and some of the people said to him: Had you given him a dirham it would have sufficed. Ibn Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Among kindness is that a man maintain the affection of his father, and this one was a friend of Umar. No one narrated this hadith from al-Wasim ibn Jamil except Qutaybah."
"8006","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Burd ibn Abi Ziyad, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi who said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever follows a funeral until prayer is offered over it, he has a qirat of reward, and whoever walks with a funeral until it is buried, he has two qirats of reward, and the qirat is like Uhud. No one narrated this hadith from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi except Burd; Abthar alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from al-Bara except with this chain."
"8007","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Simak ibn Atiyyah, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of habal al-habalah. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Zayd except Abu Kamil."
"8008","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, al-Azhar ibn Rashid narrated to us, Salim ibn Amir narrated to us, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Muadh ibn Jabal who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a cloak trimmed with silk, and said: A collar of fire on the Day of Resurrection. This hadith is not narrated from Muadh except with this chain; Ismail ibn Ayyash alone narrated it."
"8009","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Umar ibn al-Walid al-Shanni narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon on Friday, when a man entered stepping over the necks of people, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One of you comes late, then steps over the necks of people and harms them. He said: I only, upon hearing the call, performed ablution. He said: Is it a day of ablution? No one narrated this hadith from Ikrimah except Umar ibn al-Walid, nor from Umar except Bishr ibn al-Sari; Muhammad ibn Abi Umar alone narrated it."
"8010","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: Quraysh said to the Jews: Give us something we may ask this man about, so they said: Ask him about the soul, so they asked him, then there came down: They ask you about the soul; say, the soul is of the affair of my Lord, and you have not been given of knowledge except little. They said: We have been given much knowledge, then there came down: Say, if the sea were ink for the words of my Lord, the verse. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except Ibn Abi Zaidah; Qutaybah alone narrated it."
"8011","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad Buran narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) faced the rising of the sun and said: From here rises the horn of Satan, and here are tribulations and earthquakes, and the loud-voiced ones, and hardness of hearts. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Yahya, except al-Aswad. And the people narrated it: from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Salim."
"8012","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub and Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The deed of none of you will admit him into Paradise, nor save him from the Fire. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even I, except that Allah envelop me with His mercy. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Ayyub, except al-Qawariri."
"8013","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub and Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Ayyub, except Abu al-Rabi."
"8014","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sanani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, raising it, he said: The belly and drowning are martyrdom. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except al-Tufawi; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala alone narrated it."
"8015","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya Abu Ghassan al-Kinani narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn Abdullah al-Hizami informed me, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah said: Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to me, Nafi narrated to me, from Ibn Umar who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you come to Friday, perform ghusl. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Nafi, except Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah, nor from Abd al-Aziz except Mundhir ibn Abdullah, nor from al-Mundhir except Abu Ghassan al-Kinani; Muhammad ibn Yahya alone narrated it. And the people narrated it from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, without Nafi in it."
"8016","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abadah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a land called Adharah, so he named it Khadirah. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Abadah."
"8017","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Hatim ibn Wardan narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of the conquest, and found him branding the camels he had acquired as spoils. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except Hatim ibn Wardan and Ibn Abi Adi."
"8018","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Awf, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Two qualities do not combine in a hypocrite: good appearance and understanding in religion. No one narrated this hadith from Awf except Khalaf ibn Ayyub; Abu Kurayb alone narrated it."
"8019","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mihran al-Jammal narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Awf, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever kills a covenanted person without right, he will not find the scent of Paradise, and its scent is found from a distance of one hundred years. No one narrated this hadith from Awf except Isa ibn Yunus."
"8020","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mihran al-Jammal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Salamah al-Makki mentioned, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: A gift was given to Aishah and Hafsah while they were fasting, so they ate from it, and mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Make up a day in its place, and do not return. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Muhammad ibn Abi Salamah; Muhammad ibn Mihran alone narrated it."
"8021","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn al-Zubayr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever draws his sword then puts it down, his blood is wasted. No one among those who narrated it from Mamar mentioned Ibn al-Zubayr in this hadith except al-Fadl ibn Musa. And Abd al-Razzaq and others narrated it disconnected."
"8022","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, Asim ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ashjai narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd narrated to us, from Salamah ibn al-Akwa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one swears at the pulpit a false oath except that he takes his seat in the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd except Asim ibn Abd al-Aziz; Abu Musa al-Ansari alone narrated it."
"8023","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Abd al-Mumin ibn Abdullah Abu al-Hasan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Khalid al-Absi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muqarrin al-Muzani narrated to us, from Ghalib ibn Abdullah ibn Abjar who said: I mentioned Qays before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on Qays, may Allah have mercy on Qays. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, you ask mercy for Qays? He said: Yes, he was upon the religion of my father Ismail ibn Ibrahim, the close friend of Allah. O Qays, greet Yemen; O Yemen, greet Qays. Qays are the horsemen of Allah on earth. By the One in whose hand is my soul, there will come upon people a time when there is no supporter for this religion other than Qays. Allah has horsemen from the people of heaven marked, and horsemen from the people of earth known; so the horsemen of Allah from the people of earth are Qays. Qays is but an egg that split from us, the people of the house. Qays are the lions of Allah, meaning the lions of Allah. This hadith is not narrated from Ghalib ibn Abjar except with this chain; Qutaybah alone narrated it."
"8024","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Saksaki, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa who said: Some people of the Arabs said: O Messenger of Allah, we accepted Islam and did not fight you, while sons of so-and-so fought you, so Allah sent down: They consider it a favor to you that they accepted Islam; say, do not consider your Islam a favor to me, the verse. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn al-Saksaki except Hajjaj, nor from Hajjaj except Hafs; Sahl ibn Uthman alone narrated it."
"8025","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Isa ibn Salim al-Shashi narrated to us, Abu al-Malih al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Umar, that he divorced his wife during her menstruation, and that reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he commanded him to take her back, and not to touch her until she becomes pure; when she becomes pure, if he wishes he may divorce, and if he wishes he may keep. No one narrated this hadith from Maymun ibn Mihran except Abu al-Malih."
"8026","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj; Ibrahim ibn Tahman alone narrated it."
"8027","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not supplicate for death, nor wish for it; whoever supplicates, let him say: O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is better for me, and cause me to die when death is better for me. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except al-Hajjaj; Ibrahim ibn Tahman alone narrated it."
"8028","And with it, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking and eating in vessels of gold and silver. No one narrated this hadith from Anas ibn Sirin except al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj; Ibrahim ibn Tahman alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from Anas ibn Malik about the prohibition of eating and drinking in vessels of gold and silver except with this chain."
"8029","And with it, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: O Living, O Sustainer. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except al-Hajjaj; Ibrahim ibn Tahman alone narrated it."
"8030","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Azdi narrated to us, Abu Tumaylah narrated to us, from Abu Taybah, Abu Mijlaz narrated to us, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wears silk or drinks from silver is not from us, and whoever alienates a woman against her husband, or a slave against his masters, is not from us. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain; Abu Tumaylah alone narrated it."
"8031","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Shawdhab narrated to us, Amir ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Ahwal narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) acquired spoils, he would command Bilal, who would call among the people three times for the people to come with their spoils, so we would take the fifth and divide it. Then a man came to him after that with a bridle of hair, and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is of what we acquired of the spoils. He said: Did you not hear Bilal calling three times? He said: Yes. He said: What prevented you from bringing it? He offered excuse to him, so he said: Be the one who brings it on the Day of Resurrection, for I will not accept it from you. No one narrated this hadith from Amir al-Ahwal except Abdullah ibn Shawdhab."
"8032","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muslim ibn Abi Muslim al-Jarmi narrated to us, Makhlad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Let none of you say: I sowed, but let him say: I plowed. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Makhlad; Muslim al-Jarmi alone narrated it."
"8033","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Mufaddal ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) departed before the sun declined, he would delay Zuhr to the time of Asr, then descend and join between them; if the sun declined before he departed, he would pray Zuhr, then ride. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Uqayl."
"8034","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham and Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Cool down with prayer in severe heat, for severe heat is from the breath of Hell, or he said: from the opening of the gates of Hell. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Ayyub, except al-Qawariri."
"8035","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Man ibn Isa narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas who said: The most beloved color to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was green. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Said ibn Bashir, nor from Said except Man; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir alone narrated it."
"8036","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhriz ibn Awn narrated to us, Quran ibn Tammam narrated to us, from Ayman ibn Nabil, from Qudamah ibn Abdullah ibn Ammar al-Amiri who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulating the House on his camel, touching the Stone with his staff. No one narrated this hadith from Ayman except Quran ibn Tammam."
"8037","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuman narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that a man came to Umar and said: I divorced my wife irrevocably while she was menstruating. Umar said: You disobeyed your Lord and separated from your wife. The man said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not command Ibn Umar, when he separated from his wife, to take her back? Umar said to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to take her back with a divorce still remaining for him, and there has remained nothing for you by which to take back your wife. No one narrated this hadith with this wording, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, except Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi; al-Tarjuman alone narrated it."
"8038","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muslim ibn Amr al-Hadhdha al-Madini narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not make your houses graves, nor make my grave a festival, and send blessings upon me, for your blessings reach me wherever you are. None gave this hadith connected from Ibn Abi Dhib except Abdullah ibn Nafi; Muslim ibn Amr alone narrated it."
"8039","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to accept the gift and reward for it. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Isa ibn Yunus."
"8040","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Hafs ibn Abdullah Abu Umar al-Darir al-Hulwani narrated to us, Umar ibn Ubayd, seller of khumur, narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah loves that His concessions be taken as He loves that His obligations be taken. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Umar ibn Ubayd; Abu Umar al-Darir alone narrated it."
"8041","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Abu Bakr ibn Salim, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take a house in the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl except Qutaybah."
"8042","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah ibn Ubaydullah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw in the hand of a man a ring of gold, so he struck his finger with a stick he had until he threw it away. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Anas, except Ibrahim ibn Sad, and Abd al-Aziz al-Umari alone narrated it. And al-Numan ibn Rashid narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Thalabah al-Khushani."
"8043","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Numan ibn Rashid narrating, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir who said: The Jews said: When he covers his wife from behind, his child comes cross-eyed, then there came down: Your women are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth however you wish, whether from behind or otherwise, except that it is in one opening. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except al-Numan, nor narrated it from al-Numan except Jarir; Wahb ibn Jarir alone narrated it."
"8044","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Attaf ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on a khumrah. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Nafi, except Attaf; Qutaybah alone narrated it."
"8045","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahib al-Harithi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to place one of his feet upon the other while reclining. No one narrated these two hadiths from Amr ibn Dinar except Muhammad ibn Muslim; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahib alone narrated them."
"8046","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, Musa ibn Yaqub informed me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Ibn Shihab, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Suraqah, from Busr ibn Said, that Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever equips a warrior has like his reward, and whoever takes care of a warrior among his family has like his reward. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, nor from Abd al-Rahman except Musa ibn Yaqub; Ibn Abi Fudayk alone narrated it."
"8047","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Yusuf ibn al-Majishun narrated to us, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Kab ibn Malik, from Aishah, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, who are your wives in Paradise? He said: You are among them, so it seemed to me that he did not marry a virgin other than me. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn Kab ibn Malik except al-Majishun, nor narrated it from al-Majishun except his son Yusuf; Muhammad ibn Bakkar alone narrated it."
"8048","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Musa al-Taymi narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while in Madinah, saying: O Allah, put in it double the blessing of Makkah. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Usamah ibn Zayd, nor narrated it from Usamah except Abdullah ibn Musa al-Taymi."
"8049","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we love people whose deeds we do not reach? He said: You are with whom you love. The people said: And we likewise, O Messenger of Allah? He said: You are likewise. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj; Ibrahim ibn Tahman alone narrated it."
"8050","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Abu Ayyub who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The place of a whip in Paradise is better than what is between heaven and earth."
"8051","And with it, from Abu Ayyub, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kisra will perish and there will be no Kisra after him, for he says: I am the king of kings; and Qaysar will perish and there will be no Qaysar after him, for he says: I am the king of kings. No one narrated these two hadiths from Qatadah except al-Hajjaj; Ibrahim ibn Tahman alone narrated them."
"8052","And with it, from al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Abd al-Ala ibn Abd Rabbihi, that he narrated to him that he heard Abu Hurayrah narrating, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Isa will descend, break the cross, and kill the pig. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except al-Hajjaj; Ibrahim ibn Tahman alone narrated it."
"8053","And with it, from al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fears Allah enters Paradise, enjoying in it, not suffering misery, living and not dying, his clothes not wearing out, his youth not perishing. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj and Hisham al-Dastuwai; Ibrahim ibn Tahman alone narrated it from al-Hajjaj, and Muadh ibn Hisham alone narrated it from his father."
"8054","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Humayd ibn Masadah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Habib narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from Ibn Umar who said: The sunnah is that a man perform ghusl at his ihram and when he enters Makkah. No one narrated this hadith from Bakr except Humayd; Sufyan ibn Habib alone narrated it."
"8055","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yunus and Simak ibn Atiyyah and Hisham, among others, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abd al-Rahman, do not ask for leadership, for if you are given it upon asking, you are left to it, and if you are given it without asking, you are helped in it; and when you swear an oath and see another better than it, do what is better and expiate your oath. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Zayd except Abu Kamil."
"8056","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us, Suwayd Abu Hatim narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Salman ibn Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: With the boy is his aqiqah, so shed blood for him, remove harm from him; charity upon the poor is charity, and your charity upon your kin is two charities. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah, from Hafsah bint Sirin, except Suwayd Abu Hatim. And others narrated it: from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin."
"8057","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Maqabiri narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, this hadith, then I met Mansur ibn al-Mutamir and asked him about it, so he narrated to us, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that he said about recitation behind the imam: Be silent for the recitation as you were commanded, and the imam will suffice you that. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Abd al-Wahhab; Yahya ibn Ayyub alone narrated it."
"8058","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, he said: I heard my father, Abu Hamzah narrated to us, Asim ibn Sulayman informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik: that the cup of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke, so he put a silver chain in place of the crack. No one narrated this hadith from Asim, from Ibn Sirin, except Abu Hamzah."
"8059","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, from Waki ibn Udus, from Abu Razin, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked questions and criticized them, but when Abu Razin asked him, that pleased him and he answered him. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Salamah except Muammal; al-Muqaddami alone narrated it."
"8060","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Sad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji narrated to us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the earnings of a slave woman except that she have a known lasting work. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ala except Muslim; Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam alone narrated it."
"8061","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Salt ibn Masud al-Jahdari narrated to us, Malik ibn Sulayman Abu Ghassan al-Nahshali narrated to us, from Yazid al-Dabbi, from Anas ibn Malik, raising it, he said: Do not exploit a slave woman except a slave woman skilled with her hands. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid al-Dabbi except Malik ibn Sulayman; al-Salt alone narrated it."
"8062","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, my aunt Hammadah bint Muhammad narrated to me, from her aunt Aminah bint Abd al-Rahman, from her grandmother Umm Layla, who said: We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and among what he took upon us was that we dye deeply, comb with honey, and not leave our hands without dye."
"8063","And with it, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us, when one of us can take for her hands two bracelets of silver, and if she cannot, she should bind her hands even with a strap. And he said: Do not resemble men. These two hadiths are not narrated from Umm Layla except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Imran alone narrated them."
"8064","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Awwal narrated to us, Abu Tumaylah Yahya ibn Wadih narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from his uncle Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not wish to meet the enemy, you do not know what will be in that. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ishaq except Abu Tumaylah."
"8065","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzaz narrated to us, Abu Shihab al-Hannat narrated to us, from Ismail, from Qays, from Jarir who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he looked at the moon on the night of full moon, and said: You will see your Lord openly as you see this, not wronged in seeing Him; so if you can not to be overcome over a prayer before sunrise and before sunset, then do. Then he recited: And glorify with praise of your Lord before sunrise and before sunset. None among those who narrated the hadith from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid said: You see your Lord openly, except Abu Shihab; Khalaf alone narrated it."
"8066","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad and al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, they said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, Ayyub and Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not a liar who reconciles between people, saying good or conveying good. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Wuhayb."
"8067","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zunbur narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the reward of ribat, so he said: Whoever stands guard a night protecting from behind the Muslims has like the reward of those behind him who fasted and prayed."
"8068","And with it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give charity, for charity is your ransom from the Fire. No one narrated these two hadiths from Humayd except al-Harith ibn Umayr; Muhammad ibn Zunbur alone narrated them."
"8069","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas, that Sad came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother died and did not bequeath; will it benefit her if I give charity for her? He said: Yes, and upon you is water. Musa ibn Harun said: Marwan erred in it at Makkah; it is from Humayd, from al-Hasan."
"8070","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Thabit narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: No prophet ever had a wet dream; wet dreams are only from Satan. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn al-Husayn except Ibn Abi Habibah, nor from Ibn Abi Habibah except Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Thabit; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir alone narrated it."
"8071","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Awwal narrated to us, Abu Tumaylah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah al-Ataki, from Ata, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded fasting Ashura. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Ubaydullah al-Ataki; Abu Tumaylah alone narrated it."
"8072","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take suhur, for in suhur is blessing. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Layla except al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad."
"8073","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Maymun al-Saigh narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, that Aishah informed him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed while she was lying across before him."
"8074","And with it, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah who said: In every prayer is recitation, even with the Fatihat al-Kitab; what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited aloud to us, we recite aloud, and what he recited silently, we recite silently. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ibrahim al-Saigh except Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat and Awn ibn Mamar."
"8075","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Atiyyah ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, from al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman al-Taymi, from Muhammad ibn Fada, from his father, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade breaking the current coin of the Muslims among them except from harm. No one narrated this hadith from Baqiyyah except his son."
"8076","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Harun ibn Dawud al-Nakhkhar al-Tarsusi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Alhani narrated to us, from Abu Umamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites Ayat al-Kursi after every prescribed prayer, nothing prevents him from entering Paradise except that he dies. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ziyad except Muhammad ibn Himyar, and it is not narrated from Abu Umamah except with this chain."
"8077","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Musab ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father Abdullah narrated to me, from my grandfather Musab ibn Thabit, from Hanzalah ibn Qays, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr and Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Kurayz, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed, or he said: whoever dies, defending his wealth is a martyr. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Amir except with this chain; Abdullah ibn Musab ibn Thabit alone narrated it."
"8078","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim and Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, they said: Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Yaqub, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) killed Abdullah ibn Khatal on the day of the conquest; they brought him out from under the curtains of the Kabah, and struck his neck between Zamzam and the Maqam. He said: No Qurashi shall be killed after him in captivity. This hadith is not narrated from al-Saib ibn Yazid except with this chain; Abu Mashar alone narrated it."
"8079","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Musab narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Isa ibn Umar ibn Musa, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed itikaf, his bedding and bed were placed for him at the pillar of repentance toward the qiblah, then he would lean upon it. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Isa ibn Umar; al-Darawardi alone narrated it."
"8080","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Halabi narrated to us, Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Ruzayq, from Mansur, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no woman whose husband asks her for a need and she refuses, so he sleeps angry with her, except that the angels curse her until morning. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Ammar ibn Ruzayq; Abu al-Jawwab alone narrated it."
"8081","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Harun ibn Sad, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The molar of the disbeliever in the Fire, or the canine of the disbeliever, is like Uhud, and the thickness of his skin is a journey of three. No one narrated this hadith from Harun ibn Sad except Hasan ibn Salih, nor from Hasan except Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman."
"8082","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Asim ibn Hakim, from Yahya ibn Abi Amr al-Shaybani, from his father, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Pray in the resting places of sheep, and do not pray in the resting places of camels. This hadith is not narrated from Uqbah ibn Amir except with this chain; Ibn Wahb alone narrated it."
"8083","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Kulayb ibn Wail, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade buying fruit until its soundness appears. No one narrated this hadith from Kulayb ibn Wail except Sharik; Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim alone narrated it."
"8084","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, that Umar said to the six: they are those from whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left the world while pleased with them. He said: Pledge to whomever Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf pledges to; when you pledge to whomever Abd al-Rahman pledges to, whoever refuses, strike his neck."
"8085","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, that Umar entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while a man was massaging his back, so Umar asked him, and he said: The she-camel tired me last night, or as he said. No one narrated these two hadiths from Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Aslam except Qutaybah."
"8086","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed one tawaf for his Hajj and Umrah. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik except Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad."
"8087","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: None remained with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud except four, one of them Abdullah ibn Masud. No one narrated this hadith from Salamah except his son."
"8088","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Makhzumi narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prayer for one without ablution, and no ablution for one who does not mention the name of Allah over it. No one narrated this hadith from Yaqub ibn Salamah except Muhammad ibn Musa al-Makhzumi, and he is al-Fitri."
"8089","And with it: from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Friday has an hour no sincere servant meets it supplicating Allah except that He answers him. None among those who narrated this hadith from Abu Hurayrah said: sincere servant, except Salamah Abu Yaqub with this chain; Muhammad ibn Musa alone narrated it."
"8090","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Mufaddal ibn Fudalah, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Sulaym ibn Amr ibn al-Ahwas who said: Umm Jundub narrated to me that she saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the jamrah, saying: Let not some of you kill others, and throw with pebbles like those of khadhf. No one narrated this hadith from Mufaddal ibn Fudalah except Hammad ibn Zayd."
"8091","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam al-Urani narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Harb narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Waqid, from Said ibn Abi Said, freedman of al-Mahri, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A nation entered Paradise altogether, who would not seek ruqyah, nor cauterize, and upon their Lord they relied. No one narrated this hadith from Said, freedman of al-Mahri, except Uthman ibn Waqid; Shuayb ibn Harb alone narrated it."
"8092","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, Asim ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ashjai narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Qunfudh al-Taymi narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Silan, from Ibn Masud, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a man who performs ghusl from janabah and misses water on part of his body? He said: Let him wash that place, then pray. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Masud except with this chain; Abu Musa al-Ansari alone narrated it."
"8093","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever covers a fault of his brother, it is as if he gave life to a buried girl. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Abu Mashar; Abu al-Rabi alone narrated it."
"8094","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Kamil ibn Talhah al-Jahdari narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Do not ask for leadership, for if you are given it without asking, you are helped in it, and if you are given it upon asking, you are left to it; and when you swear an oath and see another better than it, do what is better and expiate your oath. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Ashhab except Kamil ibn Talhah."
"8095","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, Asim ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ashjai narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of gharar. No one narrated this hadith from al-Harith except Asim; Abu Musa alone narrated it."
"8096","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: We used to pray Friday with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then return and take midday rest. No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl except Ahmad ibn Abdah."
"8097","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, Asim ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Abu Suhayl ibn Malik, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever looks into the house of people without their permission, it is lawful for them to poke out his eye. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Suhayl except Asim; Abu Musa al-Ansari alone narrated it."
"8098","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, Asim ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Aishah, who said: I used to pour the ablution water of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was menstruating. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman ibn Yasar except al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, nor from al-Harith except Asim ibn Abd al-Aziz; Abu Musa al-Ansari alone narrated it."
"8099","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, I heard Husayn ibn Zayd saying: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us at Makkah in Dar al-Ajalah, while Jafar ibn Muhammad was present, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah made lawful of women three: marriage with inheritance, marriage without inheritance, and possession of the right hand. Jafar did not deny it. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Husayn ibn Zayd; Abu Musa al-Ansari alone narrated it."
"8100","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Umar ibn Sayf, from al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufrah, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A fire will be sent upon the people of the east and gather them to the west; it stays with them where they stay night, and rests midday with them where they rest, having what falls from them and lags, driving them as the driving of the broken camel. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except al-Hajjaj; Ibrahim ibn Tahman alone narrated it."
"8101","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Nafi, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When three go out on a journey, let them appoint one of them."
"8102","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Nafi, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When three are on a journey, let them appoint over them one of them. No one narrated these two hadiths from Muhammad ibn Ajlan except Hatim ibn Ismail."
"8103","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Musa al-Taymi narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Abu Murarah al-Juhani, from Ibn Sir al-Duali, from his father who said: I was in the direction of Makkah, when a man came and greeted while I was among my sheep. I said: Who are you? He said: I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: Welcome to the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). What do you want? He said: I want the charity of your sheep. He said: I brought him a sheep giving birth just delivered. When he looked at it, he said: Our right is not in this. I said: In what is your right? He said: In the thaniyyah and the jadhaah. It is not narrated from Sir except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir alone narrated it."
"8104","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated to us, Suwayd Abu Hatim narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mawraq al-Ijli, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The woman is awrah, and when she leaves her house, Satan looks at her, and the closest she is to Allah is in the bottom of her house. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Suwayd Abu Hatim and Hammam and Said ibn Bashir; Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi alone narrated it from Hammam, and Abu al-Jumahir alone narrated it from Said."
"8105","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Musab ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abdullah ibn Ikrimah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek provision in the hidden things of the earth. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Hisham ibn Abdullah ibn Ikrimah; Musab al-Zubayri alone narrated it."
"8106","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us, Abu Hammam Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the house of Umm Salamah praying in a garment wrapped. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Abu Hammam."
"8107","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Attab ibn Bashir informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad except Attab; Ishaq ibn Rahawayh alone narrated it."
"8108","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman who said: I was holding the bridle of the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), leading him, while Ammar was driving him, or Ammar was leading him while I was driving him, when twelve masked men faced us. He said: These are the hypocrites until the Day of Resurrection. We said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not send to each man of them and kill him? He said: I dislike that people say Muhammad kills his companions, and perhaps Allah will suffice them with al-dubaylah. We said: What is al-dubaylah? He said: A flame of fire placed upon the heartstrings of one of them, killing him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash; Yahya ibn Adam alone narrated it."
"8109","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus informed us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged in the fetus with a ghurrah: a slave, or a slave woman, or a horse, or a mule. The one against whom judgment was passed said: Shall I pay for one who neither ate, nor drank, nor cried and uttered sound? The like of that is wasted. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He speaks with the speech of a poet; in it is a ghurrah: a slave, or a slave woman, or a horse, or a mule. None among the narrators of this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr said: or a horse, or a mule, except Isa ibn Yunus."
"8110","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah informed us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that people complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of walking, so he said: Upon you is al-nasalan. He said: So we walked swiftly and found it lighter. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Rawh ibn Ubadah, nor narrated it from Jafar except Ibn Jurayj."
"8111","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan Abu Masud al-Zajjaj al-Mawsili informed us, Mamar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that he used to soak dates alone and unripe dates alone, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Soak each one of them alone. No one narrated this hadith from Mamar except Abu Masud al-Zajjaj."
"8112","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about withdrawal, so he said: Not from all water is the child; if Allah wills to create something, nothing prevents Him. None among those who narrated this hadith inserted between Abu Ishaq and Abu al-Waddak: al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash; Yahya ibn Adam alone narrated it."
"8113","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa informed us, from Abd al-Mumin ibn Khalid, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over the two socks, and prayed and made me stand on his right. None among those who narrated this hadith from al-Mughirah said: and he prayed and made me stand on his right, except Abdullah ibn Buraydah; Abd al-Mumin ibn Khalid alone narrated it."
"8114","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith informed us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed and spat in his garment and rubbed it. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Salamah except Abd al-Samad."
"8115","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir informed us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq saying: Abdullah ibn Abi Najih narrated to me, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: It was obligated upon them that one fight ten, so that was heavy upon them and hard upon them, so He reduced from them to one man fighting two men. Allah sent down about that: If there are of you twenty patient, they overcome two hundred, to the end of the verses. Then He said: Had it not been for a decree from Allah that preceded, there would have touched you for what you took a great punishment, meaning: had I not punished one who disobeys Me until I warn him. Then He said: O Prophet, say to those in your hands of captives, the verse. Al-Abbas said: By Allah, it came down about me, when I informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of my Islam, and asked him to reckon me with the twenty uqiyyahs I took with me, so he gave me for them twenty slaves, all trading with my wealth in his hand, along with what I hope of the forgiveness of Allah, exalted His mention. No one narrated this hadith with this completeness from Muhammad ibn Ishaq except Jarir ibn Hazim; Wahb ibn Jarir alone narrated it."
"8116","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Yahsabi narrated to me, my father narrated to me, from Habib ibn Maslamah who said: I heard Abu Dharr saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: If my ummah does not steal from spoils, no enemy will ever stand against them. Abu Dharr said to Habib ibn Maslamah: Does the enemy stand against you for the milking of a sheep? He said: Yes, and three fat sheep. Abu Dharr said: You have stolen, by the Lord of the Kabah. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Dharr except with this chain; Baqiyyah alone narrated it."
"8117","Musa narrated to us, Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: I heard Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed Qarn for the people of Iraq. I said: Who narrated to you this, O Abu Abdullah? He said: Nafi, from Ibn Umar. Abd al-Razzaq said: Some people of Madinah said to me: Malik erased this hadith from his book. No one narrated this hadith from Malik except Abd al-Razzaq; Ishaq ibn Rahawayh alone narrated it."
"8118","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, he said: I said to Abu Usamah: Did Abu Rawq narrate to you? And his name is Atiyyah ibn al-Harith. Salih ibn Abi Tarif narrated to me, he said: I asked Abu Said al-Khudri, saying to him: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying about this verse: Perhaps those who disbelieved will wish they were Muslims? He said: Yes, I heard him saying: Allah brings out people of the believers from the Fire, after taking His vengeance from them. And he said: When Allah admits them into the Fire with the polytheists, the polytheists say to them: You claim you are the allies of Allah in the world, so what is with you that you are with us in the Fire? When Allah hears that from them, He permits intercession for them; the angels and the prophets intercede, and the believers intercede, until they come out by the permission of Allah. When the polytheists see that, they say: Would that we were like them, so intercession would reach us and we come out with them. He said: That is the saying of Allah: Perhaps those who disbelieved will wish they were Muslims. They will be named in Paradise al-Jahannamiyyin because of blackness in their faces. They will say: O Lord, remove from us this name. He will command them to bathe in a river of Paradise, and that name goes from them. Abu Usamah acknowledged it and said: Yes."
"8119","Musa narrated to us, Ishaq narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Zayd ibn Yuthay, from Hudhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Bakr, what if you found with Umm Ruman a man, what would you do? He said: I would do evil to him. Then he said: O Umar, what if you found a man, what would you do? He said: By Allah, I would kill him. He said: And you, O Suhayl ibn Bayda? He said: May Allah curse the far one, for he is wicked, and may Allah curse the far woman, for she is wicked, and may Allah curse the first of the three, he mentioned. He said: O Ibn Bayda, you interpreted the Quran: And those who accuse their wives, to the end of the verse. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except his son Yunus."
"8120","Musa narrated to us, Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Umar ibn Sad ibn Abi Husayn al-Nawfali narrated to us, that Ali ibn Abdullah al-Adawi informed him, that his father informed him, he said: I heard Muawiyah on the pulpit saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade gold and silk. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Abdullah al-Adawi except Ibn Abi Husayn; Abdullah ibn al-Harith alone narrated it."
"8121","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik: a funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he stood up. It was said: It is the funeral of a Jew. He said: We only stood up for the angels. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hammad ibn Salamah, and none narrated it from Hammad except al-Nadr ibn Shumayl and Yahya ibn Abbad, from Qatadah."
"8122","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there is a palace of pearl with no crack in it and no flaw; Allah has prepared it as a hospitable abode for His close friend Ibrahim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Simak except Hammad ibn Salamah, and none narrated it from Hammad except al-Nadr ibn Shumayl and Yazid ibn Harun."
"8123","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus informed us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with (Sabbih isma rabbika al-a'la) and (Qul ya ayyuha al-kafirun) and (Qul huwa Allahu ahad), and when he gave the salutation he said: Subhan al-Malik al-Quddus, three times, prolonging his voice with the last one, and saying: Rabb al-mala'ikah wa al-ruh. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah; Isa ibn Yunus is alone in transmitting it."
"8124","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her when she was six years old, and consummated the marriage with her when she was nine years old. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ajlah except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, and none from Abu Bakr except Yahya ibn Adam; Ishaq ibn Rahawayh is alone in transmitting it."
"8125","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Usayd ibn Hudayr, he said: While I was praying one night I saw light like lanterns descending from the sky; when I saw that I fell prostrate. I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Why did you not continue, O Abu Atik? He said: When I saw it I could do nothing but fall prostrate. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had you continued you would have seen wonders; those are the angels descending for the Quran. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hisham, and none from Hisham except Mu'adh; Ishaq ibn Rahawayh is alone in transmitting it."
"8126","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Kamil ibn Talhah al-Jahdari narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Bukayr ibn Abd Allah al-Ashajj narrated to me, from Abu Bakr ibn al-Munkadir, from Abu Salamah, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissed while he was fasting. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Bakr ibn al-Munkadir except Bukayr ibn Abd Allah; Layth ibn Sa'd is alone in transmitting it."
"8127","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Kamil ibn Talhah al-Jahdari narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Abu Ma'bad narrated to me, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn al-Husayn: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be four tribulations: a tribulation in which blood is made lawful, the second in which blood and wealth are made lawful, and the third in which blood, wealth and private parts are made lawful. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan except Abu Ma'bad; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"8128","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Kamil ibn Talhah al-Jahdari narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abd al-Samad Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, his Companions sat grieving, weeping around him. Then a tall, handsome, eloquent man came, wearing a waist-wrapper and a cloak, hairy on the shoulders and chest. He stepped over the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he took hold of the two doorposts, and wept over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a while. Then he said: In Allah there is consolation for every calamity, a successor for everyone who perishes, and compensation for everything lost; so turn to Allah, and desire Him, for only he is afflicted whom reward does not console. The people said: Do you know the man? They looked right and left and saw no one. Abu Bakr said: This is al-Khidr, the brother of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith is not narrated from Anas except by this chain; Abbad ibn Abd al-Samad is alone in transmitting it."
"8129","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Kamil ibn Talhah narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Ka'b ibn Alqamah, he said: I heard Abu al-Najm, that he heard Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There will be a man from Banu Umayyah in Egypt holding authority, then he will be overcome in his authority or it will be stripped from him, then he will flee to the Romans, and the Romans will come against the people of Islam; that will be the first of the great battles. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Dharr except by this chain; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"8130","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Kamil narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, from Urwah, from Zayd ibn Thabit: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing of fruit is to be bought until its soundness appears, and that is when the red blush is distinguished from the yellow. No one narrated this hadith from Urwah except Abu al-Aswad; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"8131","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Hawtharah ibn Ashras al-Minqari narrated to us, Suwayd Abu Hatim narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from his father, from his grandfather: a man said: O Messenger of Allah, which prayer is best? He said: Lengthy standing. He said: Which charity is best? He said: The effort of one of little means. He said: Which believers are most complete in faith? He said: The best of them in character. This hadith is not narrated from Umayr ibn Qatadah except by this chain; Suwayd Abu Hatim is alone in transmitting it."
"8132","Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed the tashahhud after raising his head from the two prostrations of forgetfulness. No one narrated this hadith from al-Sha'bi except Ibn Abi Layla; his son is alone in transmitting it from him."
"8133","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Yazid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays one rak'ah of the dawn prayer before the sun rises, and one rak'ah after it has risen, has caught the prayer; and whoever catches two rak'ahs of the afternoon prayer before the sun sets, and two rak'ahs after it has set, has caught it, meaning al-Asr. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except al-Zubaydi, and none from al-Zubaydi except Yazid ibn Yusuf; Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim is alone in transmitting it."
"8134","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Samti narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Mujalid narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Bara ibn Azib: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say the takbir at every lowering and rising. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Isma'il ibn Mujalid."
"8135","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Habib al-Kufi, known as Ibn al-Mayyitah, narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muslim al-Mula'i narrated to us, from Abu al-Jahhaf, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the door of Ali for forty mornings after he had visited Fatimah, and said: Peace be upon you, people of the house, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; the prayer, may Allah have mercy on you: (Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, people of the house, and to purify you thoroughly). No one narrated this hadith from Abd Allah ibn Muslim al-Mula'i except Ibrahim ibn Habib."
"8136","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ali ibn Isa al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A spring will flow from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection, saying: I am charged with three: every obstinate tyrant, whoever sets another god with Allah, and whoever kills a soul without (right of) a soul. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, and none from Fudayl except his son; none narrated it from Muhammad ibn Fudayl except Ali ibn Isa al-Makhzumi and Muhammad ibn Hafs ibn Rashid al-Hilali."
"8137","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Miskin ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Hurrah, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best water on the face of the earth is the water of Zamzam, in it is nourishment from food and cure from sickness; and the worst water on earth is water in the valley of Barahut near Hadramawt, upon it like the legs of locusts of vermin, flowing in the morning and with no moisture in it by evening. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Abi Hurrah except Muhammad ibn Muhajir, and none from Muhammad except Miskin ibn Bukayr; al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shu'ayb is alone in transmitting it."
"8138","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty says: When I take the two precious things of a servant and he is patient, seeking reward, his recompense is nothing but Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Ali ibn Mushir; Sahl ibn Uthman is alone in transmitting it."
"8139","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the minbar, and when he placed his foot on a step he said: Amen, then he ascended and said: Amen, then he ascended and said: Amen. He said: Jibril came to me and said: Whoever reaches the month of Ramadan and dies without being forgiven, may Allah distance him; say: Amen. He said: And whoever reaches his two parents or one of them and dies without being forgiven, may Allah distance him; say: Amen. He said: And whoever is mentioned before him and does not send blessings upon you, may Allah distance him; say: Amen. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Hafs; Sahl ibn Uthman is alone in transmitting it."
"8140","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa informed us, from al-Husayn ibn Waqid, from Ilba ibn Ahmar al-Yashkuri, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and the time of sacrifice came, so we sacrificed a camel on behalf of ten. No one narrated this hadith from Ilba ibn Ahmar except al-Husayn ibn Waqid."
"8141","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad, meaning Ibn Aishah, narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from Raja ibn Haywah, he said: I heard Maslamah ibn Makhlad saying: While I was in charge of Egypt, the chamberlain doorkeeper came and said: A bedouin on a camel is at the door seeking permission. I said: Who are you? He said: Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari. He said: I looked down upon him and said: Shall I come down to you or will you come up? He said: Neither come down nor shall I come up; a hadith reached me which you narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about concealing the believer, and I have come to hear it. I said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever conceals (the fault of) a believer, it is as if he gave life to a buried girl. Then he struck his camel and returned. No one narrated this hadith from Raja ibn Haywah except Abu Sinan; Ibn Aishah is alone in transmitting it."
"8142","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, Ash'ath ibn Abd al-Malik informed us, from al-Hasan, from Sa'd ibn Hisham, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rak'ahs after witr while sitting. No one narrated this hadith from Ash'ath except al-Nadr."
"8143","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dye his hair? He said: He did not reach the need for dyeing; there were white hairs in his beard. I said: Did Abu Bakr dye? He said: Yes, with henna and katam. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Isma'il ibn Zakariyya."
"8144","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Habib al-Mu'allim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to leave Ibn Umm Maktum in charge of Madinah, leading the people in prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Habib al-Mu'allim except Yazid ibn Zuray'; Umayyah is alone in transmitting it."
"8145","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Ziyad ibn Riyah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hasten to do deeds before six: the Dajjal, the Smoke, the Beast of the earth, the rising of the sun from its west, the general affair, and the private affair of each one of you. No one narrated this hadith from Shu'bah except Yazid ibn Zuray'; Umayyah is alone in transmitting it."
"8146","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Bishr ibn Hilal al-Sawwaf narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man dozes while praying, let him leave, for perhaps while supplicating in his prayer he may supplicate against himself without knowing. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Abd al-Warith."
"8147","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Kamil ibn Talhah al-Jahdari narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Ramadan enters, all the gates of Paradise are opened, and none of them is closed until the end of the month; the gates of the Fire are locked, and none of them is opened until the end of the month; the rebellious devils are chained; and Allah has freed people at the time of every breaking of fast, whom He frees from the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, except Yunus; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it. And the people narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Abi Anas, from Abu Hurayrah."
"8148","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Kamil ibn Talhah al-Jahdari narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Bakr ibn Sawadah narrated to us, from Abu Umayyah al-Jumahi: a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the Hour, and he said: Among its signs are three, one of them: seeking knowledge from the young. Musa said: It is said that the young are the people of innovation. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Umayyah al-Juhami except by this chain; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"8149","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Kamil narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, that he visited Zaynab bint Abi Salamah and she narrated to him: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with Umm Salamah; he carried Hasan on one side, Husayn on the other side, and Fatimah in his lap, and said: (The mercy of Allah and His blessings upon you, people of the house; indeed He is Praiseworthy, Glorious). This hadith is not narrated from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah except by this chain; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"8150","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Kamil narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr: Aishah said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast. No one narrated this hadith from Amr except Ibn Lahi'ah and al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah."
"8151","And with the same chain Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abd Allah ibn Amr: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw upon him a garment dyed with safflower and said: What is this? So Abd Allah went and burned it with fire. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What did you do with your garment? He said: I burned it. He said: Why did you not clothe someone with it? No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib except Amr ibn Shu'ayb; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"8152","Musa narrated to us, Kamil narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to me, Nafi' ibn Sulayman al-Makki narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sulaym, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mihran, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: One who waits for prayer after prayer is like a horseman whose horse gallops with him in the path of Allah with its full flank; the angels pray for him so long as he does not break his ablution or stand up, and he is in the greater ribat. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mihran except Yahya ibn Sulaym, and none from Yahya except Nafi' ibn Sulayman; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"8153","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, al-Furat ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, he said: I set out with my father to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we found him with his waist-wrapper loosened; my father circled behind him and placed his hand upon the Seal. No one narrated this hadith from al-Fudayl ibn Talhah except al-Furat ibn Abi al-Furat."
"8154","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus informed us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor of a house has the most right to the house. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas, except Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah; Isa ibn Yunus is alone in transmitting it. And with Isa there is also the hadith of Qatadah from al-Hasan from Samurah."
"8155","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah informed us, from his uncle Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Bukht, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, he said: I saw Jabir ibn Abd Allah and Jabir ibn Umayr al-Ansari shooting arrows; one of them tired and sat down, and the other said to him: Have you grown lazy? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Everything that is not from the remembrance of Allah is diversion and heedlessness, except four traits: a man's walking between the two targets, his training his horse, his playing with his family, and learning swimming. This hadith is not narrated from Jabir ibn Abd Allah and Jabir ibn Umayr except by this chain; Muhammad ibn Salamah is alone in transmitting it."
"8156","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Hakkam ibn Salm narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far al-Razi, from Layth, from Mundhir, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no blame except in killing a Muslim, three times. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah except Mundhir, and none from Mundhir except Layth, and none from Layth except Abu Ja'far, and none from Abu Ja'far except Hakkam; Ishaq ibn Rahawayh is alone in transmitting it."
"8157","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Khayyat narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Layth, from Mundhir al-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, he said: Abu Hurayrah informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah; when they say it, their wealth and blood become inviolable to me, and their reckoning is upon Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah except Mundhir, and none from Mundhir except Layth, and none from Layth except Sharik; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan is alone in transmitting it."
"8158","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, Asim ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ashja'i narrated to us, Nubayt ibn Umar al-Ansari and Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim al-Madani narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ma'mar ibn Abd Allah al-Adawi: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None hoards except a sinner. No one narrated this hadith from Nubayt ibn Umar and Abd al-Rahman except Asim ibn Abd al-Aziz; Abu Musa al-Ansari is alone in transmitting it."
"8159","Musa narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, Abu Kurz narrated to us, Nafi' narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go out to the two Eids with a spear and a shield. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Kurz except Ali ibn al-Ja'd."
"8160","Musa narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Mujalid narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about Abu Talib, whether he benefited him? He said: I brought him out from Hell to a shallow part of it."
"8161","And with the same chain from Jabir: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about Khadijah, that she died before the obligations and rulings were revealed, and he said: I saw her upon a river from the rivers of Paradise, in a house of reed, in which there is no idle talk and no fatigue. Neither of these two hadiths was narrated from al-Sha'bi except by Mujalid; Isma'il ibn Mujalid is alone in transmitting them."
"8162","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Jud'an, from al-Hasan, from Ibn Mughaffal: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has eaten food and walked in the marketplaces, meaning the Dajjal. Thus Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated it from Sufyan, saying: from Ibn Mughaffal. And al-Humaydi and Ali ibn al-Madini and others narrated it from Sufyan, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn."
"8163","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Isma'il al-Mu'addib narrated to us, from Ya'qub ibn Ata, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you eats of this plant, let him not harm us in our mosque."
"8164","And with the same chain from Ya'qub, from his father, from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a woman: Perform umrah in Ramadan, for an umrah in Ramadan suffices you in place of a Hajj. Neither of these two hadiths was narrated from Ya'qub ibn Ata except by Abu Isma'il al-Mu'addib; Surayj is alone in transmitting them."
"8165","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Bashir ibn al-Muhajir, from Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would hardly laugh more than until we saw, or his molars appeared. No one narrated this hadith from Bashir ibn al-Muhajir except Hatim."
"8166","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Hatim narrated to us, from Bashir ibn al-Nu'man, from Sayyar, from Tariq, from Ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Before the Hour, usury and wine will appear. No one narrated this hadith from Bashir ibn al-Nu'man except Hatim."
"8167","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Burjumi narrated to us, he said: I heard Thabit al-Bunani narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has daughters or three sisters, and fears Allah and maintains them, will be with me in Paradise like this. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Burjumi except Shayban."
"8168","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed on a road, and a black woman passed, and a man said to her: The road! She said: The road is there. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave her, for she is obstinate."
"8169","And with the same chain from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When he entered Makkah, Abd Allah ibn Rawahah walked before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying verses. Umar said: O Ibn Rawahah, before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and in the Sanctuary of Allah you speak poetry? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him alone, O Umar, for by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, this is harder upon them than the striking of swords. Neither of these two hadiths was narrated from Thabit except by Ja'far ibn Sulayman."
"8170","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Salm ibn Qutaybah Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Abi Hazm narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite the Quran from its beginning to its end in the obligatory prayers. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Suhayl; Abu Qutaybah is alone in transmitting it."
"8171","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Hashim narrated to us, Hanbal ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from Abu Talhah, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a campaign, and he met the enemy, and I heard him saying: Master of the Day of Judgment, You alone we worship, and from You alone we seek help. He said: I saw men being struck down, the angels striking them from before them and from behind them. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Talhah except by this chain; Abu al-Rabi' is alone in transmitting it. I heard Musa ibn Harun saying: I asked Uthman ibn Talut about Hanbal, and he said: They claimed he is a man from Banu Quray'. And I asked him about Abd al-Salam ibn Hashim, and he said: An old Basran shaykh. I said to him: Was he trustworthy? He said: I know nothing but good."
"8172","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abd al-Majid ibn Suhayl, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah: A man from the Ansar freed a slave of his after his death, while he was needy. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he called him and said: Did you free your slave? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are in greater need of him. Then he said: Who will buy him? Nu'aym ibn Abd Allah said: I will. So he bought him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took its price and gave it to its owner. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Majid except al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman; Qutaybah is alone in transmitting it."
"8173","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhriz ibn Awn narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashja'i, from Abu Husayn al-Asadi, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, he said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a donkey, and he said to me: O Mu'adh, what is the right of Allah upon the servants? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: That they worship Him and associate nothing with Him. Then he said: O Mu'adh, what is the right of the servants upon Allah if they do that? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: That He not punish them. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Malik except Khalaf ibn Khalifah."
"8174","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Umar ibn Zurarah al-Hadathi narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Uthman al-Balawi, from Asim ibn Abi al-Baddah ibn Asim ibn Adi, from his grandfather Asim ibn Adi, he said: My brother and I bought one hundred shares from the shares of Khaybar; that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O Asim, two hungry wolves let loose upon sheep whose owner has neglected them are no more corrupting to them than a man's love of wealth and honor is to his religion. This hadith is not narrated from Umayrah bint Sahl except by this chain; Isa ibn Yunus is alone in transmitting it."
"8175","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Umar ibn Zurarah al-Hadathi narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Uthman al-Balawi narrated to us, from his grandmother, the daughter of Adi: Her mother Umayrah bint Sahl, the Companion of the two sa's whom the hypocrites mocked, narrated to her that he went out with his zakat, a sa' of dates, and with his daughter Umayrah, until he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and poured it out. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a need of you? He said: And what is it? He said: That you supplicate Allah for me and for her for blessing, and wipe her head, for I have no child but her. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hand upon me, and I swear by Allah it was as if the coolness of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon my liver. This hadith is not narrated from Umayrah bint Sahl except by this chain; Isa ibn Yunus is alone in transmitting it."
"8176","And with the same chain Isa narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Uthman al-Balawi, from Urwah ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from his father, from Husayn ibn Wahwah: When Talhah ibn al-Bara met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O Messenger of Allah, command me with whatever you love, and I will not disobey any command of yours. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marveled at that, though he was a boy, and said to him then: Go and kill your father. He turned away to do it, so he called him and said to him: Come back, for I have not been sent to sever kinship. Talhah later fell ill, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit him in winter, in cold and cloud. When he left he said to his family: I do not think but that death has come upon Talhah; inform me so that I may attend him and pray over him, and hasten. Before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached Banu Salim ibn Awf, he died, and night fell. Among what Talhah said was: Bury me, and join me to my Lord, blessed and exalted, and do not call the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for I fear for him the Jews, and that he may be harmed on my account. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed in the morning, so he came and stood at his grave, and the people lined up with him, and he said: O Allah, meet Talhah while You smile to him and he smiles to You. This hadith is not narrated from Husayn ibn Wahwah except by this chain; Isa ibn Yunus is alone in transmitting it."
"8177","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Yusuf al-Sha'ir narrated to us, Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Friday there is an hour which no Muslim meets while praying, asking Allah for good therein, except He gives it to him. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, except Ammar ibn Ruzayq; Abu al-Jawwab is alone in transmitting it. And Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad narrated it from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah, without mentioning Ibn Abbas."
"8178","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the prescribed one."
"8179","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, Amr narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yasar, he said: I heard Tawus; Hajr al-Madari informed me, from Zayd ibn Thabit: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed concerning the umra gift that it belongs to the one given it for his life and his death."
"8180","And with the same chain from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: A man said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), my mother died without a will; will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf? He said: Yes. None of these hadiths was narrated from Muhammad ibn Muslim except by Dawud ibn Amr."
"8181","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: Umar stood at Mina and asked the people: Who has knowledge of the inheritance of a woman from the blood-money of her husband? Al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan al-Kilabi stood and said: Enter your tent until I inform you. He entered, and he came to him and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to me to give the wife of Ashyam al-Dibabi her inheritance from the blood-money of her husband. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Sa'id except Ibn Abi Za'idah; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah is alone in transmitting it."
"8182","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Ruzayq, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Yahya, from Ibn Abbas: (If he belonged to a people hostile to you and he is a believer, then the freeing of a believing slave). He said: A man would come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and embrace Islam, then return to his people and remain among them while they were polytheists, and the Muslims would strike him by mistake in a detachment or battle, so the one who struck him would free a slave; (And if he belonged to a people with whom you have a covenant). He said: He is a man under covenant whose people are people of covenant; the blood-money is delivered to them, and the one who struck him frees a slave. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Yahya, except Ammar ibn Ruzayq; Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham is alone in transmitting it."
"8183","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuman narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Safwan narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Sharik ibn Tariq, from Farwah ibn Nawfal, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The pilgrim in ihram kills five vermin: the crow, the mouse, the vicious dog, and the kite. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr except Shu'ayb ibn Safwan; al-Tarjuman is alone in transmitting it."
"8184","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Humaysi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should milk anyone's livestock except with his permission; would one of you like that his storeroom be come to, its door broken, and what is in it plundered? For what is in the udders of their cattle is the food of one of them. Abu Ishaq al-Humaysi narrated nothing from Ayyub, from Nafi', other than this; he is alone in transmitting it, al-Himmani alone from him."
"8185","Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Sayrafi narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Abu al-Ashhab, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The begging of a rich man is a blemish on his face. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Ashhab except Waki'; Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Wahhab is alone in transmitting it."
"8186","Musa narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to me, from Ya'qub ibn Mujammi' ibn Jariyah, from his father: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out in the funeral of a man from Banu Amr ibn Awf until he reached the graveyard, and said: Peace be upon the people of the graves, three times; whoever among you was of the believers and Muslims, you are predecessors for us and we follow you; may Allah grant us and you well-being. This hadith is not narrated from Mujammi' ibn Jariyah except by this chain; Dawud ibn Amr is alone in transmitting it."
"8187","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worst of people in theft is he who steals his prayer. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how does he steal his prayer? He said: He does not complete its bowing and its prostration. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except al-Walid, and none narrated it from al-Walid except al-Hakam ibn Musa and Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti."
"8188","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Harun ibn Muslim al-Ijli al-Basri narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Qatadah, he said: My father came to me while I was bathing on Friday, and said: Is this bathing of yours from janabah or for Friday? I said: From janabah. He said: Repeat with another bathing, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever bathes on Friday remains in purity until the next Friday. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Aban, and none from Aban except Harun ibn Muslim."
"8189","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, he said: I visited Umar ibn al-Khattab, and I took hold of the two doorposts while he was laid out, and said: How do you see him? They said: As you see. I said: Wake him with the prayer, for you will not wake him with anything more alarming to him than the prayer. They said: The prayer, O Commander of the Believers. He said: The prayer, yes, by Allah then; and there is no share in Islam for whoever abandons prayer. So he prayed while his wound gushed blood. No one narrated this hadith from Qurrah ibn Khalid except Wahb ibn Jarir."
"8190","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Nasr al-Tammar narrated to us, Uqbah al-Asamm narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade looking into the stars. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Uqbah al-Asamm."
"8191","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, Musa ibn Uthman al-Hadrami narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Zayd ibn Arqam and al-Bara ibn Azib: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Musa ibn Uthman; Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih is alone in transmitting it."
"8192","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Sahl ibn Zanjalah al-Razi narrated to us, al-Sabbah ibn Muharib narrated to us, from Harun ibn Antarah, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Umar, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I broke fast one day in Ramadan. He said: Without excuse or travel? He said: Yes. He said: Evil is what you did. He said: Yes; what do you command me? He said: Free a slave. He said: By Him Who sent you with the truth, I have never owned a slave. He said: Then fast two consecutive months. He said: I cannot do that. He said: Then feed sixty poor persons. He said: By Him Who sent you with the truth, I do not even satiate my family. He said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a basket containing dates, and said: Give this in charity to sixty poor persons. He said: To whom shall I give it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: To the poorest you know. He said: There is no household more needy than us. He said: Then take it back to your dependents. No one narrated this hadith from Habib except Harun; al-Sabbah ibn Muharib is alone in transmitting it."
"8193","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Anbasah al-Abdi, from al-Hasan: Abu Bakrah entered the mosque while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was bowing, so he bowed and then walked until he joined the row. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: May Allah increase you in eagerness, but do not repeat. No one narrated this hadith from Anbasah except Wuhayb; al-Abbas al-Narsi is alone in transmitting it."
"8194","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Qurran ibn Tammam narrated to us, from al-A'mash, he said: Anas ibn Malik said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed of Laylat al-Qadr, and he came intending to inform us of it, but heard noise in the mosque. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Qurran."
"8195","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Karabisi narrated to us, Zanfal ibn Shaddad al-Arafi, from the people of Arafah, narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrating from Aishah, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The signs of hypocrisy: whoever, when he speaks, lies; when he is entrusted, betrays; and when he promises, breaks. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Bakr except by this chain; Sa'id ibn Abd al-Jabbar is alone in transmitting it."
"8196","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Abu Sinan Isa ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Shaddad ibn Aws, he said: Mu'awiyah mentioned fleeing from the plague in his sermon, and Ubadah said: Your mother Hind knows better than you. He completed his sermon, then prayed, then sent for Ubadah; men from the Ansar went with him, and he detained them and Ubadah entered. Mu'awiyah said to him: Did you not fear Allah and feel shame before your imam? Ubadah said: Do you not know that I pledged to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of al-Aqabah that I do not fear the blame of any blamer for the sake of Allah? Then Mu'awiyah went out at Asr, prayed Asr, then took hold of the minbar post and said: O people, I mentioned to you a hadith upon the minbar, then I entered the house and found the hadith as Ubadah narrated to me; so take from him, for he is more understanding than I."
"8197","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Isa ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Shaddad ibn Aws, from Ubadah, he said: The first to practice withdrawal were a group of the Ansar; they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: A group of the Ansar practice withdrawal. He was alarmed and said: The created soul will come to be, so I neither command nor forbid. Neither of these two hadiths was narrated from Ya'la ibn Shaddad ibn Aws except by Abu Sinan, and none from Abu Sinan except Abu Usamah; Ishaq ibn Rahawayh is alone in transmitting them."
"8198","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Salih ibn Qudamah al-Madani informed us, Abd Allah ibn Dinar narrated to me, he said: Nafi' said: Abd Allah ibn Umar used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you dies, his seat is presented to him morning and evening; if he is of the people of Paradise, or of the people of the Fire, it is said: This is your seat until Allah resurrects you on the Day of Resurrection."
"8199","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Salih ibn Qudamah informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Nafi', he said: Abd Allah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade traveling with the Quran to the enemy, fearing the enemy would get hold of it."
"8200","And with the same chain, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, he said: Nafi' said: When Abd Allah prayed in congregation, he would leave for his house and pray two prostrations, and say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do that. None of these hadiths was narrated from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Nafi', except by Salih ibn Qudamah."
"8201","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Daghfal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Upon the Christians was the fast of the month of Ramadan; they had a king who fell ill, and they said: If Allah heals him we shall add eight days. Then they had a king after him who ate meat and fell sick, and they said: If Allah heals him we shall add eight days. Then they had a king after him who said: We shall not leave any of these days but complete them, and make our fast in spring. So he did, and it became fifty days. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hisham; Mu'adh is alone in transmitting it."
"8202","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah informed us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained in Makkah thirteen years, and died at the age of sixty-three. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Zakariyya ibn Ishaq; Rawh is alone in transmitting it."
"8203","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim informed us, from Marzuq ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from Ka'b ibn Malik, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from pursuing the Confederates, and alighted at Madinah, he laid down his armor, bathed, and used incense. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Marzuq ibn Abi al-Hudhayl; al-Walid ibn Muslim is alone in transmitting it."
"8204","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Kamil, from Nasr ibn Alqamah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn A'idh, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you narrate to people about their Lord, do not narrate to them what frightens them and is hard upon them. This hadith is not narrated from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib except by this chain; Baqiyyah is alone in transmitting it."
"8205","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa informed us, from Husayn ibn Waqid, from Yahya ibn Uqayl, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to remember Allah much, engage little in idle talk, prolong prayer, shorten the sermon, and would not refuse to walk with a widow or a poor person to fulfill his need. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abi Awfa except by this chain; al-Fadl ibn Musa is alone in transmitting it."
"8206","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abu Ishaq al-Kufi, from al-Bara ibn Azib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah and His angels send blessings upon the front row; the caller to prayer is forgiven as far as his voice reaches, and all who hear him, moist and dry, affirm him, and he has the like of the reward of those who prayed with him. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hisham; Mu'adh is alone in transmitting it."
"8207","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Amir al-Ahwal, from al-Hasan, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning one who forgets prayer, he said: He prays when he remembers. No one narrated this hadith from Amir al-Ahwal except Hisham; Mu'adh is alone in transmitting it."
"8208","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed four in Madinah and two at Dhu al-Hulayfah, then spent the night at Dhu al-Hulayfah until morning; when he mounted his camel and it stood upright with him, he entered ihram. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Ibn Jurayj; Isa ibn Yunus is alone in transmitting it. And others than Isa narrated it from Ibn Jurayj, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir and Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Anas."
"8209","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Ibrahim ibn Murrah, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A virgin is not to be married until she is asked permission, and her permission is silence; and the previously married woman decides of her affair so long as she does not call to displeasure; if she calls to displeasure while her guardians call to approval, that is raised to the ruler. Ishaq said: I said to Isa: Is the end of the hadith from the hadith of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Thus I have it from al-Awza'i. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Ibrahim ibn Murrah, and none narrated it from Ibrahim ibn Murrah except al-Awza'i; Isa ibn Yunus is alone in transmitting it."
"8210","And with the same chain, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Qasim, from Aishah: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw rain, he said: O Allah, a wholesome, pleasant downpour. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except al-Awza'i; Isa ibn Yunus is alone in transmitting it."
"8211","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to me, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while we were all youths, and said: Upon you is marriage; whoever cannot, upon him is fasting, for it is a restraint for him. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham, from al-Hasan, from Anas, other than Baqiyyah."
"8212","Musa narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Abd Allah ibn Sa'd, from al-Sunabihi, from Mu'awiyah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade difficult tangled questions. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh said: Rawh narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, he said: Tangled questions are hard problems and severe ones. No one narrated this hadith well-mastered from al-Awza'i except Isa ibn Yunus."
"8213","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith informed us, he said: I heard my father narrating, Hasan ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever asks a question out of ample wealth thereby increases for himself coals of Hell. They said: What is ample wealth? He said: A night's supper. No one narrated this hadith from Habib ibn Abi Thabit except al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan, and none from al-Hasan except Abd al-Warith; Abd al-Samad is alone in transmitting it."
"8214","Musa narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah informed us, from Sallam ibn Subayh, from Mansur ibn Zadham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Tribes were mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they asked him about Banu Amir, and he said: A bright camel eating from the edges of trees. And they asked him about Hawazin, and he said: Blossoms following their water. And they asked him about Banu Tamim, and he said: Firm of foot, weighty of counsel, great of heads; the severest of people against the Dajjal at the end of time; a red plateau which those who oppose it do not harm. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Sirin except Mansur, and none from Mansur except Sallam ibn Subayh; Abu Mu'awiyah is alone in transmitting it."
"8215","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not marry among the Ansar? He said: They have intense jealousy. No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah except Hammad ibn Salamah; al-Nadr ibn Shumayl is alone in transmitting it."
"8216","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Thumamah informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night in Ramadan; people came and stood behind him, and he prayed lightly, then entered his house and prayed, then came out and prayed lightly. In the morning they said: O Messenger of Allah, we stood behind you in the night, and you would enter your house then come out. He said: I only did that for your sake. No one narrated this hadith from Thumamah except Hammad ibn Salamah; al-Nadr is alone in transmitting it."
"8217","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): My mother has died; will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf? He said: Yes. He said: I have a garden of date-palms, and I call you to witness that I have given it in charity on her behalf. Rawh said: A makhrafah is date-palms. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Zakariyya ibn Ishaq and Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Ta'ifi."
"8218","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had two freed slaves: an Abyssinian and a Copt. One day they reviled one another while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) listened; one of them said to his companion: O Abyssinian! And the other said: O Copt! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not say this, for you are both two men of the household of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah except Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, and none from Yazid except Abu Hafs al-Abbar; Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim is alone in transmitting it."
"8219","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah informed us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Its thorny trees are not to be cut, its game is not to be driven away, its herbage is not to be gathered, and its lost property is not lawful except for one who announces it. Al-Abbas said: Except idhkhir? He said: Except idhkhir. No one narrated this hadith from Zakariyya ibn Ishaq except Rawh."
"8220","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani informed us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Hariz, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade marrying a woman together with her paternal aunt and maternal aunt. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Sa'id; Muhammad ibn Bakr is alone in transmitting it."
"8221","Musa narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi informed us, Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sa'd; Yazid said: I think it is from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say when he said: Allah hears him who praises Him: O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will after. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Ibrahim except Abu Amir al-Aqadi; the well-known version is from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Qays."
"8222","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed us, Hisham narrated to me, from Ata, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not bring his wife into the bathhouse; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not sit at a table over which wine is passed around, or he said: over which wine is drunk. It is said: This is Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, and Allah knows best. None narrated it from Ata except Hisham, and none from Hisham except Mu'adh; Ishaq is alone in transmitting it."
"8223","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Aws ibn Abd Allah ibn Buraydah narrated to me, from his father, from Buraydah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Buraydah, there will be expeditions; be in the expedition of Khurasan, and settle in the city of Marw, for Dhu al-Qarnayn built it and supplicated for blessing for it; no evil will ever befall its people. This hadith is not narrated from Buraydah except by this chain; Aws ibn Abd Allah is alone in transmitting it."
"8224","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Imran ibn Husayn: A boy of poor people cut the ear of a boy of rich people, so they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he assigned them nothing. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hisham; Mu'adh is alone in transmitting it."
"8225","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Haywil al-Misri narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Mas'ud ibn al-Hakam, from Abd Allah ibn Hudhafah al-Sahmi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to announce in the days of Mina: None shall fast in these days, for they are days of eating and drinking and remembrance of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Qurrah; Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz is alone in transmitting it."
"8226","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Azhar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abd Allah ibn Babayah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah Almighty boasts to His angels on the evening of Arafah, saying: My servants have come to Me disheveled and dusty. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id; Azhar is alone in transmitting it."
"8227","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah al-A'ma, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: While I was praying, a devil confronted me, so I seized his throat and strangled him until I felt the coldness of his tongue upon my hand; had it not been for the supplication of my brother Sulayman, he would have remained tied up for you to look at. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd Allah except Husayn, and none from Husayn except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash; Yahya ibn Adam is alone in transmitting it."
"8228","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhimari narrated to us, Fa'id ibn Umar narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: A woman used to pick litter from the mosque, then she died, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not informed of her burial. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you dies, inform me. He prayed over her and said: I saw her in Paradise for picking litter from the mosque. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam ibn Aban except Fa'id ibn Umar; al-Dhimari is alone in transmitting it."
"8229","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever looks into the house of a people without their permission and they put out his eye, there is no blood-money upon them and no retaliation. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hisham; Mu'adh is alone in transmitting it."
"8230","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yaman informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Muslim, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): My nation are bright-faced and bright-limbed from the traces of ablution. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Yahya ibn Yaman."
"8231","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Sha'ir narrated to us, Sahl ibn Hammad Abu Attab al-Dallal narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, the son-in-law of Malik ibn Dinar, from Malik ibn Dinar, from Thumamah ibn Abd Allah ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken up, he passed by people whose lips were being cut with scissors, and said: O Jibril, who are these? He said: These are the preachers from your nation who command people to righteousness and forget themselves, while they recite the Book; will they not reason? No one narrated this hadith from al-Mughirah except Hisham, and none from Hisham except Abu Attab and Yazid ibn Zuray'; Yazid ibn Zuray' did not mention Thumamah in his hadith."
"8232","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn al-Hanafi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no divorce except after marriage, and no emancipation except after ownership. No one narrated this hadith except Abu Bakr ibn al-Hanafi and Waki' - and Waki' did not say in his hadith: nor emancipation except after ownership. And none narrated it from Abu Bakr al-Hanafi except Muhammad ibn al-Minhal."
"8233","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of what you treat yourselves with is cupping and costus from the sea. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Sa'id; Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata is alone in transmitting it."
"8234","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Buhlul ibn Muwarriq narrated to us, Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed me, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: Al-Zubayr was a blind man, and Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Al-Zubayr passed by me on the day of Bu'ath and freed me; give him to me so I may repay him. He said: He is yours. He said to al-Zubayr: Do you know me? He said: Yes, you are Thabit. He said: I bestow upon you as you bestowed upon me on the day of Bu'ath. He said: Will that benefit me? Where is my family? He returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Give me his family. He gave him his family, and he came to him and informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had returned his family to him. He said: O son of my brother, what use is it to live as bodies? Where is the wealth? He returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, give me his wealth. He said: And his wealth is yours. He returned to him and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has returned your wealth to you, and Allah has intended good for you. He said: O son of my brother, what happened to Huyayy ibn Akhtab, chief of the settled and the nomads? He said: He was killed. He said: O son of my brother, what happened to Zayd ibn Buta, protector of the Jews? He said: He was killed. He said: O son of my brother, what happened to Ka'b ibn Ashta, at whose handsomeness the maidens of the tribe marveled? He said: He was killed. He said: What happened to the two assemblies? He said: They are as yesterday gone. He said: Between me and meeting the loved ones is only as the emptying of a bucket; I ask you by my hand upon you to join me to the people. So he killed him. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Musa ibn Ubaydah, and none from Musa except Buhlul ibn Muwarriq."
"8235","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Harith al-Harrani narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib ibn Abi Balta'ah: He narrated that his father wrote a letter to the disbelievers of Quraysh while he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), though he had witnessed Badr. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Ali and al-Zubayr and said: Go until you meet a woman with a letter; bring it to me. They went until they met her, and said: Give us the letter you have; and they told her they would not leave until they stripped every garment from her. She said: Are you not two Muslim men? They said: Yes, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told us you have a letter. When she was certain they would not let her go, she loosened the letter from her head and gave it to them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Hatib until he read the letter to him, and said: Do you recognize this letter? He said: Yes. He said: What carried you to that? He said: My children and kin are there, and I was a stranger among you, O company of Quraysh. Umar said: Permit me to kill Hatib? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No; he witnessed Badr, and you do not know: perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do whatever you wish, I have forgiven you. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Ishaq ibn Rashid; Ubayd Allah ibn Amr is alone in transmitting it."
"8236","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Sha'ir narrated to us, Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Nafi' ibn Umar al-Jumahi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, from Marwan ibn al-Hakam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The earth is the earth of Allah, and the servants are the servants of Allah; whoever revives dead land, he has the most right to it. This hadith is not narrated from Marwan except by this chain; Hajjaj ibn al-Sha'ir is alone in transmitting it."
"8237","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from Sa'id ibn Zayd: He was the tenth of ten with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon Hira, and Hira shook. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be firm, O Hira, for there is none upon you but a Prophet, or a truthful one, or a martyr. Sa'id said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying after that: Abu Bakr is in Paradise, Umar is in Paradise, Uthman is in Paradise, Ali is in Paradise, Talhah is in Paradise, al-Zubayr is in Paradise, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf is in Paradise, and Sa'd is in Paradise. Al-Mughirah said to Sa'id: Mention to us who is the ninth? He said: Leave me; he kept at it until he said: I am the ninth. No one narrated this hadith from Adi ibn Thabit except Ali ibn Zayd, and none from Ali except al-Hajjaj; Ibrahim ibn Tahman is alone in transmitting it."
"8238","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abd Allah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, he said: We mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which is better: the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or the mosque of Bayt al-Maqdis? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in my mosque is better than four prayers therein; and it is an excellent place of prayer. And a time will soon come when a man having the like of his bow-string's length of land from where he can see Bayt al-Maqdis will be better for him than the world and what is in it. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except al-Hajjaj and Sa'id ibn Bashir; Ibrahim ibn Tahman is alone in transmitting it from al-Hajjaj, and Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud is alone in transmitting it from Sa'id."
"8239","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Idris ibn Umar, the scribe of al-Humaydi, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ibrahim, of the offspring of Jubayr ibn Mut'im, narrated to us, Umm Uthman bint Sa'id, my grandmother, narrated to me, from her father Sa'id ibn Muhammad, from his father Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father Jubayr ibn Mut'im, he said: I went out as a trader to Sham in the pre-Islamic age; when I was at the nearest part of Sham, a man of the People of the Book met me and said: Is there a man among you who has claimed prophethood? I said: Yes. He said: Do you know his likeness if you saw it? I said: Yes. He took me into a house with pictures in it, but I did not see the picture of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). While I was thus, a man of theirs entered upon us and said: What are you engaged in? We informed him, and he took us to his house. As soon as I entered I looked at the picture of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there was a man holding the heel of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: Who is this man grasping his heel? He said: There was no Prophet but there was a Prophet after him except this one, for there is no Prophet after him; and this is the caliph after him; and there was the description of Abu Bakr. This hadith is not narrated from Jubayr ibn Mut'im except by this chain; Muhammad ibn Idris, scribe of al-Humaydi, is alone in transmitting it."
"8240","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Maqabiri narrated to us, Ali ibn Thabit al-Harrani narrated to us, Nuh ibn Abi Bilal narrated to me, Zayd ibn Abi al-Attab narrated to me: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf informed him that he asked Aishah, Mother of the Believers, about the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: He used to pray, between the last Isha and Fajr, thirteen rak'ahs, including two rak'ahs with Fajr. I asked her about the fasting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: Most of his fasting apart from Ramadan was in Sha'ban; he would fast it or most of it. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Abi al-Attab except Nuh ibn Abi Bilal; Ali ibn Thabit is alone in transmitting it."
"8241","Musa ibn Jumhur al-Simsar al-Tinnisi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Isa narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Uthman ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Umamah ibn Sahl saying: We prayed Zuhr with Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, then we went out until we visited Anas ibn Malik and found him praying Asr. We said: O uncle, what is this prayer you have prayed? He said: Asr; it is the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which we used to pray with him. Abu Umamah ibn Sahl narrated no hadith from Anas other than this; Ibn al-Mubarak is alone in transmitting it."
"8242","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Nasr al-Antaki narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar except Abu Usamah; Abd Allah ibn Nasr is alone in transmitting it."
"8243","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Asbat narrated to us, A'idh ibn Shurayh narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He who gives out of plenty is not greater in reward than he who accepts when he is needy. No one narrated this hadith from A'idh ibn Shurayh except Yusuf ibn Asbat."
"8244","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abu Shaybah Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kindi narrated to us, from Abu al-Mughirah Ubayd Allah ibn al-Mughirah, from Abd Allah ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some people of my nation will recite the Quran and delve deeply into religion; Satan will come to them saying: If only you went to the kings and got some of their world, while keeping aloof from them with your religion. Yet that will be only as nothing is harvested from thorns except thorns; likewise nothing is harvested from nearness to them except sins. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except by this chain; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"8245","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting, and he was the most in control of his desire among you. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd Allah except Wuhayb, and none from Wuhayb except Mu'ammal; Muhammad ibn Musaffa is alone in transmitting it."
"8246","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Ali ibn Harb al-Mawsili narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Yazid al-Jarmi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who slept until morning? He said: Satan urinated in his ear. Sufyan said: In our view this is one who sleeps past the obligatory prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except al-Qasim al-Jarmi; Ali ibn Harb is alone in transmitting it."
"8247","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Hisham ibn Khalid narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Humayd, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about dough into which drops of blood fell, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating it. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz, and none from Suwayd except al-Walid; Hisham ibn Khalid is alone in transmitting it."
"8248","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Hisham ibn Khalid al-Azraq narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Qasri narrated to us, from Abu Rawq, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman has two veils. It was said: What are they? He said: The husband and the grave. He said: Which of them is better? He said: The grave. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Rawq except Khalid ibn Yazid al-Qasri; Hisham ibn Khalid is alone in transmitting it."
"8249","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Hisham ibn Khalid narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Qasri narrated to us, from Abu Rawq, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No moderate one ever became poor. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Rawq except Khalid ibn Yazid; Hisham ibn Khalid is alone in transmitting it."
"8250","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Marwan ibn Muhammad al-Tatari narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Yahya ibn Rashid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Count the crescent of Sha'ban for the sighting of Ramadan. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Yahya ibn Rashid; Marwan ibn Muhammad is alone in transmitting it."
"8251","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Nasr ibn Alqamah, from his brother Mahfuz ibn Alqamah, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever meets the enemy and is patient until he is killed or kills them will not be tried in his grave. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Ayyub except by this chain; Muhammad ibn Musaffa is alone in transmitting it."
"8252","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Umarah ibn Abi al-Sha'tha narrated to us, Sinan ibn Qays narrated to me, from Shabib ibn Nu'aym, Yazid ibn Khumayr narrated to me, Abu al-Darda narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes land with its tribute has renounced his migration; and whoever removes the yoke of a disbeliever from his neck and places it upon his own neck has turned Islam behind his back. This hadith is not narrated from Abu al-Darda except by this chain; Muhammad ibn Musaffa is alone in transmitting it."
"8253","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Jahm ibn Uthman, from Abd Allah ibn Hasan ibn Hasan, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Among what makes forgiveness obligatory is your bringing joy to your Muslim brother. This hadith is not narrated from al-Hasan ibn Ali except by this chain; Ibn Abi Fudayk is alone in transmitting it."
"8254","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Duhaym narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Yazid, from al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you enters the mosque, let him not sit until he prays two rak'ahs. No one narrated this hadith from al-Muttalib except Kathir ibn Yazid; Ibn Abi Fudayk is alone in transmitting it."
"8255","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Duhaym narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Abd Allah, from Zayd ibn Waqid, from Abu Ubayd Allah Muslim ibn Mishkam, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever binds the tribute upon his neck has disavowed Allah Almighty and His Messenger. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Waqid except Sadaqah; Amr ibn Abi Salamah is alone in transmitting it."
"8256","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Duhaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik al-Nawfali narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Ibrahim al-Raba'i, from his father, from Aishah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever grants respite to one in hardship, Allah will shade him in His shade on the Day of Resurrection; and every good deed is charity. This hadith is not narrated from Aishah except by this chain; Duhaym is alone in transmitting it."
"8257","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Duhaym narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Bakri, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Ruman, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: The lineage of people goes straight back to Ma'add ibn Adnan. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Ruman except Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Abd Allah ibn Yazid is alone in transmitting it."
"8258","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Salamah Sulayman ibn Sulaym, from Yahya ibn Jabir, from Mu'awiyah ibn Hakim, from his uncle Mikhmar ibn Mu'awiyah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no evil omen, though blessing may be in the horse, the woman and the house. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman ibn Sulaym except Isma'il ibn Ayyash."
"8259","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Attar narrated to us, Sawwar ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from Kulayb ibn Wa'il, from Ibn Umar: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever looks at his brother with a look of love, with no rancor in his heart toward him, will not blink before he is forgiven for his past sins. No one narrated this hadith from Kulayb ibn Wa'il except Sawwar ibn Mus'ab; Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Attar is alone in transmitting it."
"8260","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Hisham ibn Khalid al-Azraq narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, sent Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah in the year of al-Ramadah to divide a distribution among the Arabs; when he returned, Umar assigned him a wage of a thousand dinars, but he refused to take it. Umar said: Take it, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned that to us and we disliked it, then he commanded us to take it. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd except al-Walid ibn Muslim."
"8261","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Ali ibn Harb al-Mawsili narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Mas'udi, from al-Qasim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abd Allah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, support Islam with Umar. No one narrated this hadith from al-Mas'udi, from al-Qasim, except al-Qasim ibn Yazid al-Jarmi. And the people narrated it from al-Mas'udi, from Abu Nahshal."
"8262","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, al-Yaman ibn Adi narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man goes bankrupt and another man's property is with him intact, of which he has taken nothing, he is most entitled to his property itself; but if he had taken something from it, he is equal with the creditors. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, except al-Zubaydi, and none from al-Zubaydi except al-Yaman ibn Adi; Amr ibn Uthman is alone in transmitting it."
"8263","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Abu Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a grave fresh from burial and asked about it. It was said to him: The grave of so-and-so. He descended and prayed over it, and I was among those who prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over that grave; he said takbir four times. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Husayn except Ibrahim ibn Tahman."
"8264","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who is forbidden to the Fire? He said: The gentle, the lenient, the easy, the close. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, and none from Muhammad except al-Harith ibn Ubaydah; Amr ibn Uthman is alone in transmitting it."
"8265","Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: A man set aside wealth from his own wealth on behalf of his father; his father came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of that. He sent to him: Return to your father what you withheld from him, for you and your wealth are as an arrow from his quiver. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except al-Harith; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"8266","8266 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Ali ibn Harb al-Mawsili narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out walking between Abu Bakr and Umar, and he said: Thus shall we be raised on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd except Khalid ibn Yazid; Ali ibn Harb is alone in narrating it."
"8267","8267 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Ali ibn Harb al-Mawsili narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When supper is served and the prayer is called, begin with supper. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Hushaym; Ali ibn Harb is alone in narrating it from his father."
"8268","8268 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Ali ibn Harb narrated to us, Harun ibn Imran narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, from al-Hakam and Hammad, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah and Amr ibn Murrah, from al-Subayy ibn Ma'bad who said: I entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah together, then I met Umar, and he said: You have been guided to the Sunnah of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam and Hammad except Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud, nor from Sulayman except Harun; Ali ibn Harb is alone in narrating it."
"8269","8269 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Ali ibn Harb narrated to us, Rawh ibn Aslam narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit ibn al-Bunani, from al-Hasan, from Utayy, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When Adam died, the angels washed him with water an odd number of times, and a lahd was made for him, and they said: This is the Sunnah of Adam and his children. No one narrated this hadith in marfu' form from Hammad ibn Salamah except Rawh ibn Aslam."
"8270","8270 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Ali ibn Harb narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abd al-Jabbar, Ubaydah ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Anas ibn Malik who said: It is from the Sunnah to begin with the burial of the dead, and that earth be thrown upon him from the direction of the qiblah. No one narrated this hadith from Rabi'ah except Ubaydah, nor from Ubaydah except Amr; Ali ibn Harb is alone in narrating it."
"8271","8271 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Hisham ibn Khalid al-Azraq narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Subayh al-Murri narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Amr al-Makki, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah manifested Himself to Musa ibn Imran, seven mountains scattered; five of them are in the Hijaz and two in Yemen; in the Hijaz: Uhud, Thabir, Hira, Thawr and Warqan, and in Yemen: Hasur and Sabir. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Talhah ibn Amr."
"8272","8272 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Shuja' ibn al-Walid informed us, my father narrated to us, al-Ruhayl ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah who said: Water for ghusl was placed for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he poured with his right hand upon his left until he cleaned them both, then he poured with his right hand upon his private parts and washed them and whatever was affected until clean, then he placed his hand on the wall upon the dust, then washed it until clean, then rinsed his mouth and nose, performed wudu as for prayer, then poured water over his head and body, moved from his place, and washed his feet. No one narrated this hadith from Salamah ibn Kuhayl except al-Ruhayl ibn Mu'awiyah, nor from al-Ruhayl except Shuja'; his son is alone in narrating it."
"8273","8273 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Uthman ibn Yahya al-Qirqisani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Umar ibn Dharr, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Ali ibn Abi Talib to a people to fight them, then he sent a man after him and said: Do not leave him behind him, and tell him: Do not fight them until you call them. No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah except Umar ibn Dharr; Sufyan ibn Uyaynah is alone in narrating it."
"8274","8274 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Abu Taqi Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik al-Himsi narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Abd al-Quddus narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four are never satiated by four: an eye by looking, land by rain, a female by a male, and a scholar by knowledge. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Abd al-Salam ibn Abd al-Quddus; Abu Taqi is alone in narrating it."
"8275","8275 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Abu Taqi narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Abd al-Quddus narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Clothing displays wealth, oil removes misery, and kindness to the slave - Allah suppresses the enemy through it. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Abd al-Salam ibn Abd al-Quddus; Abu Taqi is alone in narrating it."
"8276","8276 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Kathir al-Kahili narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say upon the minbar: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him take a bath. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Kathir except Marwan."
"8277","8277 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Masruq, from Abu Bakr who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, grey hair has hastened upon you. He said: Surah al-Waqi'ah, and Amma yatasa'alun, and Idha al-shamsu kuwwirat have made me grey. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq, from Masruq, from Abu Bakr, except Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah; Abu Mu'awiyah is alone in narrating it."
"8278","8278 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Khalid, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from al-Maqburi, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever enters upon people for food to which he was not invited, and eats to satiation, eats unlawfully. No one narrated these two hadiths from Rawh ibn al-Qasim except Yahya ibn Khalid; Baqiyyah is alone in narrating them."
"8279","8279 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Mubashshir ibn Ubayd, from Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Asim, from Zirr, from Ali who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no bequest for a killer. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Hajjaj, nor from Hajjaj except Mubashshir; Baqiyyah is alone in narrating it, and it is not narrated from Ali except with this chain."
"8280","8280 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb ibn al-Abrash narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Humrah, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever performs wudu on Friday, that suffices and is good, and whoever takes a bath, bathing is better. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir except al-Dahhak."
"8281","8281 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Mistake, forgetfulness, and what they are coerced into have been lifted from my ummah."
"8282","8282 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as above."
"8283","8283 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as above."
"8284","8284 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as above. No one narrated the hadith of al-Awza'i from Ata from Ibn Abbas except al-Walid ibn Muslim. Nor did anyone narrate the hadith of Malik from Nafi' except al-Walid. Nor did anyone narrate the hadith of Ibn Jurayj except al-Walid. Nor did anyone narrate the hadith of Uqbah ibn Amir except Musa ibn Wardan, nor from Musa except Ibn Lahi'ah; al-Walid is alone in narrating it."
"8285","8285 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Abu Taqi Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Imran al-Qasir, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim quietly."
"8286","8286 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Imran al-Qasir, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying voluntary prayers upon a camel wherever it turned with him. No one narrated these two hadiths from Imran al-Qasir except Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz."
"8287","8287 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Abu Taqi Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All wealth, even if beneath seven earths, whose zakat is paid is not hoarded treasure; and all wealth whose zakat is not paid, even if visible, is hoarded treasure. No one narrated this hadith in marfu' form from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar except Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz."
"8288","8288 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Abu Taqi narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Humayd narrated to me, from Anas who said: One of the households of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed a bowl and it was lost, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) guaranteed compensation for it. No one narrated this hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording, 'so the Messenger of Allah guaranteed compensation for it,' except Humayd; Suwayd is alone in narrating it."
"8289","8289 - Musa ibn Jumhur narrated to us, Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, Musa ibn Ya'qub al-Zam'i narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn Uthman, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of qusamah. We said: What is qusamah? He said: Something shared among people from which a portion is taken away. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Sa'id except with this chain; Ibn Abi Fudayk is alone in narrating it."
"8290","8290 - Musa ibn Zakariyya al-Tustari narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Badr ibn al-Khalil, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Ibn Umar, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting, and he said: Upon you are the white days: three days of every month. No one narrated this hadith from Badr ibn al-Khalil except Isa ibn Yunus; Sulayman ibn Dawud is alone in narrating it."
"8291","8291 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, from Harithah ibn Abi Imran, from Sulayman ibn Abd Allah ibn Janab, from Asma bint Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from her father, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the sun set at Arafah, poured forth, and from Muzdalifah before sunrise. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Bakr except with this chain; al-Waqidi is alone in narrating it."
"8292","8292 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Abu Qabil, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As who said: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq wrote to Amr ibn al-As: Peace be upon you, then: Your letter has reached me mentioning the hosts the Romans have gathered; Allah did not grant us victory alongside His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through great numbers or many soldiers. We used to raid with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with only a few horses among us, taking turns upon camels; on the day of Uhud we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with only a single horse which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode; he used to make us prevail and aid us against those who opposed us. Know, O Amr, that the most obedient of people to Allah are those most hateful of disobedience; so obey Allah and command your companions to obey Him. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq as a connected narration except with this chain; al-Waqidi is alone in narrating it."
"8293","8293 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Ya'qub ibn Zayd ibn Talhah, from al-Zuhri, from Abu al-Tufayl who said: Ali disputed with al-Abbas over the siqayah, and Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah, Amir ibn Makhramah ibn Nawfal and Azhar ibn Abd Awf testified that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted it to al-Abbas on the day of the conquest. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Ya'qub ibn Zayd, nor from Ya'qub except Muhammad ibn Ja'far; al-Waqidi is alone in narrating it."
"8294","8294 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn al-Uqayli narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ata narrated to us, from Abu Ubaydah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn al-Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has chosen this religion for Himself; nothing befits your religion except generosity and good character, so adorn your religion with them. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan except Abu Ubaydah; Amr ibn al-Husayn is alone in narrating it."
"8295","8295 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Khazzaz narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek help against women through keeping them without adornment. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Sa'id, nor from Sa'id except Ismail; Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Khazzaz is alone in narrating it."
"8296","8296 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Musa, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abd al-Rahman, do not ask for leadership, for if you are given it without asking you will be aided in it, and if you are given it upon asking you will be left to it; and if you swear an oath then see something better than it, do what is better and expiate your oath. No one narrated this hadith from Isra'il except Sufyan ibn Uyaynah; al-Salt ibn Mas'ud is alone in narrating it."
"8297","8297 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jami' al-Attar narrated to us, Maslamah ibn Alqamah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Injury by a beast is without liability, a well is without liability, and in buried treasure is a fifth."
"8298","8298 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Nahar ibn Uthman narrated to us, Mas'adah ibn al-Yasa' narrated to us, Shibl ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man with dishevelled head and said: Why does one of you disfigure himself? And he gestured with his hand, meaning: Take from it. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Shibl ibn Abbad, nor from Shibl except Mas'adah; Nahar ibn Uthman is alone in narrating it."
"8299","8299 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Furat ibn Ahnaf, from Sallamah bint Nafi', from Aishah, that she was asked about nabidh, and she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade hantam, dubba and naqir vessels. No one narrated this hadith from Furat ibn Ahnaf except Muhammad ibn Fudayl."
"8300","8300 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Hatim ibn Salim narrated to us, Imran ibn Taliq narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself. No one narrated this hadith from Imran ibn Taliq except Hatim ibn Salim."
"8301","8301 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn al-Uqayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulathah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the servant intends night prayer, the angel comes to him and says to him: Rise, morning has come, so pray and remember your Lord; then Satan comes to him and says: The night is upon you and you will rise later, so sleep a while. If he rises and prays, he wakes energetic, light of body, glad of eye; but if he obeys Satan until morning, Satan urinates in his ear. No one narrated this hadith in marfu' form from al-A'mash from Abu Ishaq except Ibn Ulathah; Amr ibn al-Husayn is alone in narrating it."
"8302","8302 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Bishr ibn Sayhan narrated to us, Bakkar ibn Asim al-Laythi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Death in comparison to what comes after it is but like the butt of a goat. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Bakkar ibn Asim; Bishr ibn Sayhan is alone in narrating it."
"8303","8303 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Hatim ibn Salim narrated to us, Abu Umayyah ibn Ya'la al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Nafi' narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abd Allah ibn Jud'an: When you buy sandals, buy them new; when you buy a garment, buy it new; when you buy a riding animal, examine it well; and when a noble woman of a people is with you, honor her. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi' except Abu Umayyah ibn Ya'la; Hatim ibn Salim is alone in narrating it."
"8304","8304 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Shabab al-Usfuri narrated to us, Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no divorce before marriage, and no manumission before ownership. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Muhammad ibn Muslim, nor from Muhammad except Amr ibn Asim; Shabab is alone in narrating it."
"8305","8305 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yusuf al-Samti narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Idris al-Awdi narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them and forgot, so he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness. No one narrated this hadith from Idris except Yusuf ibn Khalid; his son is alone in narrating it."
"8306","8306 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qassas narrated to us, Abd al-A'la ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Sawwar al-Anbari, from Kulayb ibn Wa'il, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever denies qadar has denied what was revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8307","8307 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Allaf narrated to us, Isa ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abd Allah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr who said: Prayer is interrupted by: a black dog, a donkey, and a woman. So I asked Abu Dharr: What is the matter with the black dog as distinct from the red or yellow? He said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as you asked me, and he said: The black dog is a devil. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan from al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan except Isa ibn Shu'ayb; Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam is alone in narrating it, while others narrated it from Hisham from Humayd ibn Hilal without mentioning al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan."
"8308","8308 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mufaddal al-Harrani narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn Habib narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abd Allah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Did you see your Lord? He said: Light - how could I see Him. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid al-Hadhdha except al-Mundhir ibn Habib; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mufaddal is alone in narrating it."
"8309","8309 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Maslamah al-Umawi narrated to us, from Habib ibn Hassan, from Abu Wa'il, from al-Subayy ibn Ma'bad who said: I was a Christian, then I entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah, and came to Umar, and he said: You have been guided to the Sunnah of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Habib ibn Hassan except Sa'id ibn Maslamah; Bishr ibn Khalid is alone in narrating it."
"8310","8310 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Azhar ibn Marwan al-Raqashi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Shabib, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Atiyyah al-Qurazi who said: I was among those over whom Sa'd ibn Mu'adh judged; he judged concerning Banu Qurayzah that their fighters be killed and their offspring taken captive; he looked at me, and I had not yet grown pubic hair, so he joined me to the captives. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Abd al-Wahhab; Azhar ibn Marwan is alone in narrating it."
"8311","8311 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Tarif, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he cursed ten: the woman who tattoos and the one tattooed, the woman who scratches her face, the woman who joins hair and the one for whom it is joined, the eater of riba and its witness, the withholder of charity, the man who imitates women, and the woman who imitates men."
"8312","8312 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Tahir narrated to us, Bakkar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Bakrah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Bakrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, some poetry is wisdom. No one narrated this hadith from Bakkar ibn Abd al-Aziz except al-Nadr ibn Tahir."
"8313","8313 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Samman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, that his father lost his front tooth, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to bind it with gold. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Abu al-Rabi' al-Samman."
"8314","8314 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Basri narrated to us, Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, Abbad ibn Maysarah al-Minqari narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered a sermon and recited the end of al-Zumar in his sermon, and the minbar shook twice. No one narrated this hadith from Abbad ibn Maysarah from Ibn al-Munkadir from Jabir except Abu Bahr."
"8315","8315 - Musa ibn Zakariyya al-Tustari narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sallam al-Attar narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abis ibn Rabi'ah who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said upon the minbar: O people, be humble, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever humbles himself for Allah, Allah raises him, and He says: Rise, may Allah raise you; so he is great in the eyes of people and small in his own self; and whoever is arrogant, Allah breaks him, and He says: Be abased; so he is small in the eyes of people and great in his own self. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except al-Thawri; Sa'id ibn Sallam is alone in narrating it."
"8316","8316 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Salman al-Mazini narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Abu al-Asbat, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Learn from your lineages that by which you maintain your kinship ties. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Abu al-Asbat; Hatim is alone in narrating it."
"8317","8317 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn al-Uqayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulathah narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Arabi narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever says: O Allah, to You is praise; there is no god but You alone without partner; You are my Lord and I am Your servant; I have believed in You sincerely devoting religion to You; I wake upon Your covenant and promise as much as I can; I repent to You from my evil deeds and seek Your forgiveness for my sins which none forgives but You - saying that three times - whoever says it in his day, Allah forbids him to the Fire."
"8318","8318 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulathah narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Arabi informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: Visiting the sick on the first day is Sunnah; what comes after that is voluntary. No one narrated these two hadiths from al-Nadr ibn Arabi except Ibn Ulathah; Amr ibn al-Husayn is alone in narrating them."
"8319","8319 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulathah narrated to us, Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Babah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The menstruating woman watches between her and ten days; if she sees purity, she is pure; if she exceeds ten, she is mustahadah - she bathes and prays; if blood overcomes her, she stuffs, uses a pad, performs wudu for every prayer. And the postpartum woman waits between her and forty nights; if she sees purity before that, she is pure; if she exceeds forty, she is like the mustahadah - she bathes and prays; if blood overcomes her, she stuffs, uses a pad, and performs wudu for every prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah except Ibn Ulathah; Amr ibn al-Husayn is alone in narrating it."
"8320","8320 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Fudayl al-Jazari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fight and you shall gain booty, fast and you shall be healthy, travel and you shall become self-sufficient. No one narrated this hadith from Suhayl with this wording except Zuhayr ibn Muhammad."
"8321","8321 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Umar al-Khattabi narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Khalid al-Samti narrated to us, Salm ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Modesty and faith are joined in one yoke; when one of them is taken away, the other follows it. No one narrated this hadith from Ikrimah except Salm ibn Bashir; al-Samti is alone in narrating it."
"8322","8322 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yusuf al-Samti narrated to us, my father narrated to us, saying: I heard Musa ibn Uqbah narrating from Ubayd ibn Salman, from his father, from Abu Lubabah ibn Abd al-Mundhir who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about purification, and he said: No Muslim rinses his mouth but Allah forgives him every sin his tongue committed that day; nor washes his hands but Allah forgives him what his hands did that day; nor wipes his head but he becomes as on the day his mother bore him. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Uqbah except al-Samti; his son is alone in narrating it, and it is not narrated from Abu Lubabah except with this chain."
"8323","8323 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qati'i narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they said: The sun has been bewitched. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: The Hour has drawn near and the moon has split; and if they see a sign they turn away and say: Continuous magic. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except al-Bursani."
"8324","8324 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn al-Uqayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulathah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah narrated to us, saying: I heard Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz say: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Aishah, that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No hour passes by the son of Adam in which he did not remember Allah for good but he will regret it on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz except Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, nor from Ibrahim except Ibn Ulathah; Amr ibn al-Husayn is alone in narrating it."
"8325","8325 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulathah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Mu'adh, the believer is restrained by the Qur'an from much of the desire of his soul."
"8326","8326 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulathah narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim ibn Malik al-Jazari, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, may Allah be pleased with him, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rinse the mouth and nose, and the ears are part of the head. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Karim except Ibn Ulathah; Amr ibn al-Husayn is alone in narrating it."
"8327","8327 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulathah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyyah, from al-Hakam, from Hanash al-Kinani, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: O people, sacrifice and seek reward through their blood, for though blood falls to the ground, it falls into the protection of Allah, mighty and majestic. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Ghaniyyah except Ibn Ulathah; Amr ibn al-Husayn is alone in narrating it."
"8328","8328 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulathah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Ata al-Khurasani narrated to us, from his father, from Malik ibn Yukhamir, from Laqit ibn Amir Abu Razin al-Uqayli who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Razin, when a Muslim visits his Muslim brother, seventy thousand angels escort him invoking blessings upon him, saying: O Allah, as he joined him for Your sake, so join him. No one narrated this hadith from Ata al-Khurasani except his son Uthman, nor from Uthman except Ibn Ulathah; Amr ibn al-Husayn is alone in narrating it."
"8329","8329 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Jubayri narrated to us, Bishr ibn Ibrahim al-Ansari narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Makhul, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa': That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he needed to relieve himself, would tie a rag in his ring. This hadith is not narrated from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' except with this chain; al-Jubayri is alone in narrating it."
"8330","8330 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, Hafs ibn Jumay' narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abd Allah, in marfu' form, who said: Do you know which charity is best? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The best charity is a grant of benefit: one of you grants a dirham, or the back of a riding animal. No one narrates this hadith from Simak except Hafs ibn Jumay'; Umar ibn Yahya is alone in narrating it."
"8331","8331 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, Hafs ibn Jumay' narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Ansar said: Running between al-Safa and al-Marwah is from the affairs of Jahiliyyah, so Allah the Exalted revealed: Indeed al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah; whoever performs Hajj to the House or Umrah, there is no blame upon him to go round them both. No one narrated this hadith from Simak except Hafs ibn Jumay'; Umar ibn Yahya is alone in narrating it."
"8332","8332 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, Hafs ibn Jumay' narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abd Allah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give salam to his right and to his left until the whiteness of his cheek was seen: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Mughirah except Hafs; Umar ibn Yahya is alone in narrating it."
"8333","8333 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, al-Muhabbar ibn Qahdham narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The earth shall surely be filled with injustice and wrongdoing; when it is filled with injustice and wrongdoing, Allah will send a man whose name is my name; he will fill it with equity and justice as it was filled with injustice and wrongdoing. No one narrated this hadith from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah from his father except al-Muhabbar ibn Qahdham; Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar is alone in narrating it, while Ma'mar narrated it from Abu Harun al-Abdi from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah from Abu Sa'id."
"8334","8334 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Zayd ibn Akhzam al-Ta'i narrated to us, Ya'mar ibn Bishr narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Imran ibn Zayd al-Taghlibi, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I never saw the knee of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before a sitting companion of his ever, nor did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ever shake hands with anyone and withdraw his hand from his hand until he was the one who withdrew it. No one narrated this hadith from Mu'awiyah except Zayd al-Ammi, nor from Zayd except Imran ibn Zayd; Ibn al-Mubarak is alone in narrating it."
"8335","8335 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Ali ibn Ghurab narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Hudhayfah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever imitates a people is one of them. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Ali ibn Ghurab, nor from Ali except Abd al-Aziz; Muhammad ibn Marzuq is alone in narrating it."
"8336","8336 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Hayyan ibn Ubayd Allah Abu Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Between every two calls to prayer there is a prayer for whoever wishes, except Maghrib. No one narrated this hadith from Hayyan except Abd al-Wahid."
"8337","8337 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, Humayd ibn al-Qasim ibn Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf who said: When death came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they said: O Messenger of Allah, advise us. He said: I advise you concerning the first forerunners among the Muhajirin and their children after them; if you do not do so, neither sarf nor adl will be accepted from you. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Ja'far."
"8338","8338 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Abd al-A'la ibn Zayd al-Attar narrated to us, Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, Ash'ath narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin who said: Ibn Umar said: We used to see no harm in leasing land, but Rafi' mentioned from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade it. No one narrated this hadith from Ash'ath from Ibn Sirin from Ibn Umar except Abu Bahr; Abd al-A'la ibn Zayd is alone in narrating it."
"8339","8339 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Jumahi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ziyad Abu al-Miqdam narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no liability after four days, and the two traders have the choice so long as they have not parted. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan from Abu Hurayrah except Hisham ibn Ziyad."
"8340","8340 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn al-Uqayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulathah narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Makhul, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no household from whom no warrior goes forth, nor one who equips a warrior with a thread, a needle, or its worth in silver, nor one who takes good care of his family, but Allah afflicts them with a calamity before the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz except Ibn Ulathah; Amr ibn al-Husayn is alone in narrating it."
"8341","8341 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn al-Uqayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulathah narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Arabi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever intends a matter and consults a Muslim man concerning it, Allah guides him to the most rightful of his affairs. No one narrated this hadith from al-Nadr ibn Arabi except Ibn Ulathah; Amr ibn al-Husayn is alone in narrating it."
"8342","8342 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulathah narrated to us, from Burd, from Makhul, from Abu Umamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is jihad in the path of Allah, for it is a gate among the gates of Paradise through which Allah removes worry and grief. No one narrated this hadith from Burd except Ibn Ulathah; Amr ibn al-Husayn is alone in narrating it."
"8343","8343 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulathah narrated to us, from Wasil, freedman of Abu Uyaynah, from Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like, when he travelled on a journey, to set out on Thursday. No one narrated this hadith from Wasil except Ibn Ulathah; Amr ibn al-Husayn is alone in narrating it."
"8344","8344 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Suwayd Abu Hatim narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Artah and Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that when the dead was placed in the grave he used to say: In the name of Allah, and upon the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Suwayd Abu Hatim except Shayban."
"8345","8345 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Azhar ibn Marwan al-Raqashi narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Nabhan narrated to us, from Ma'mar ibn Rashid, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to kiss while fasting. No one narrated this hadith from Ammar except Ma'mar; al-Harith is alone in narrating it."
"8346","8346 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Ibrahim al-Jarudi narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Arzami narrated to us, from Abu Qays, from Hudhayl ibn Shurahbil, from Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, that a man assigned to a man in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a share of his wealth; then the man died without knowing what it was, so the matter was raised to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he assigned to him a sixth of his wealth. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Qays except al-Arzami; Abu Bakr al-Hanafi is alone in narrating it, and it is not narrated as connected from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"8347","8347 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, Amr ibn Hamzah narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn Tha'labah narrated to us, Abu al-Ala ibn al-Shikhkhir narrated to us, from al-Bara ibn Azib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met me, took my hand and shook it; I said: O Messenger of Allah, I thought handshaking was only among the non-Arabs. He said: We are more entitled to handshaking than them; no two Muslims meet and one takes the hand of his companion with love and sincerity but Allah casts their sins between them. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Ala Yazid ibn Abd Allah except al-Mundhir ibn Tha'labah; Amr ibn Hamzah is alone in narrating it."
"8348","8348 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Tahir narrated to us, Suwayd Abu Hatim narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take condiment from this tree, meaning: olive oil, and apply kohl with this ithmid, for it clears the vision; and whoever is offered perfume, let him take some of it. No one narrated this hadith from Layth from Mujahid except Suwayd Abu Hatim."
"8349","8349 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Bishr ibn Mu'adh al-Aqadi narrated to us, al-Sakan ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwai, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Muhayyisah al-Ansari who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the earnings of the cupper - may I eat it? He said: No. I said: May I feed orphans in my care with it? He said: No. Then he permitted him to feed his watering camel with it."
"8350","8350 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Bishr ibn Mu'adh al-Aqadi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Ata narrated to us, from Ikrimah ibn Ammar, from Salim, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your smiling in the face of your brother is charity, your removing harm from the road is recorded for you as charity, your pouring into your brother's bucket is charity, your enjoining good and forbidding evil is charity for you, and your guiding one who is lost is charity. No one narrated this hadith from Ikrimah ibn Ammar from Salim except Ibn Abi Ata; Bishr ibn Mu'adh is alone in narrating it, while others narrated it from Ikrimah ibn Ammar from Malik ibn Zayd from his father from Abu Dharr."
"8351","8351 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khulayd al-Hanafi narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When your brother tells you something, it is a trust with him, even if he did not ask you to keep it secret. No one narrated this hadith from Ja'far except Ayyub ibn Waqid; Muhammad ibn Khulayd is alone in narrating it."
"8352","8352 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn al-Uqayli narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ata narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Iyad, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ammar ibn Yasir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good character is the greatest character of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Yazid ibn Iyad, nor from Yazid except Ibrahim ibn Ata; Amr ibn al-Husayn is alone in narrating it."
"8353","8353 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn al-Uqayli narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim al-Qasmali narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Salman who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the heart of the believer trembles in the path of Allah, his sins fall away as the date-cluster of the palm falls. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Abd al-Aziz; Amr ibn al-Husayn is alone in narrating it."
"8354","8354 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Hilal ibn Bishr al-Mazini narrated to us, Umayr ibn Imran al-Allaf narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Utbah narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Amr ibn Wathilah or Amir ibn Wathilah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Hakim ibn Hizam a dinar and ordered him to buy a sacrificial animal with it; he bought, then one who profited him came and he sold, then bought again, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a dinar and a sheep. He said: What is this? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I bought, sold, and profited. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: May Allah bless your trade; he took the dinar and gave it in charity, and took the sheep and sacrificed it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Harith ibn Utbah except Umayr ibn Imran."
"8355","8355 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Sadusi narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Khalid al-Samti narrated to us, Kathir ibn Qarawanda narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I were to take a close friend, I would take Abu Bakr as a close friend, but your companion is the close friend of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Kathir except Yusuf ibn Khalid; Muhammad ibn Uqbah is alone in narrating it, and none narrated it from Adi ibn Thabit except Kathir ibn Qarawanda."
"8356","8356 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humran narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Sa'd al-Katib who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you name, say takbir - meaning: over the slaughtered animal. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman ibn Sa'd except Muhammad ibn Humran; al-Shadhakuni is alone in narrating it."
"8357","8357 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn al-Uqayli narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abd al-Malik and Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Makhul, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he began prayer, used to say: Glory be to You O Allah and with Your praise, blessed is Your name, exalted is Your grandeur, and there is no god but You. No one narrated this hadith from Makhul except Sa'id ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan and Ibn Jabir, nor from them except Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Malik; Amr ibn al-Husayn is alone in narrating it, and it is not narrated from Wathilah except with this chain."
"8358","8358 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulathah narrated to us, from Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah, from Abd Allah ibn Babah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has blessings with certain people which He keeps with them so long as they attend to the needs of people; so long as they do not tire of them, but when they tire of them He transfers them from them to others. No one narrated this hadith from Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah except Ibn Ulathah; Amr ibn al-Husayn is alone in narrating it."
"8359","8359 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khidash narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three men from those before you went out - then he mentioned the long hadith of the cave. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani except Hammad ibn Zayd, nor from Hammad except Khalid ibn Khidash; his son is alone in narrating it."
"8360","8360 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn al-Uqayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulathah narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Alqamah ibn Shihab, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever did not attain ghazw with me, let him raid by sea. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz except Ibn Ulathah; Amr ibn al-Husayn is alone in narrating it."
"8361","8361 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulathah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Ata al-Khurasani narrated to us, from his father, from Malik ibn Yukhamir, from Abu al-Darda who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is taking concubines, for they are blessed of wombs. This hadith is not narrated from Abu al-Darda except with this chain; Amr ibn al-Husayn is alone in narrating it."
"8362","8362 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Habib ibn Abi Amrah and al-A'mash, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): There are no days of this world in which deeds are better than the days of tashriq. A man said: Not even their like in the path of Allah? He repeated it three times, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him the third time: Except for one who does not return. No one narrated this hadith from al-Thawri except Hassan ibn Ibrahim."
"8363","8363 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Isa narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If she discharges as a man discharges, ghusl is upon her; if she does not discharge, nothing is upon her. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus ibn Ubayd except Abd Allah ibn Isa; Uqbah ibn Mukram is alone in narrating it."
"8364","8364 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Qalusi narrated to us, Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Ubayd Allah al-Kurayzi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Tammam narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Walid Abu Bishr, from Bishr ibn Shaghaf, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing is more honored to Allah than the believer. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Ubayd Allah ibn Tammam, nor from Ubayd Allah except Abd al-Ghaffar al-Kurayzi."
"8365","8365 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He forbade selling years in advance."
"8366","8366 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Talq ibn Sakan narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded concerning zakat al-fitr: a sa' of dates or a sa' of barley. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Talq ibn Sakan, nor from Talq except al-Qa'nabi; Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Muqaddami is alone in narrating it."
"8367","8367 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Abu Burayd Amr ibn Yazid al-Jarmi narrated to us, Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Muslim narrated to us, Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Umm Salamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world is sweet and green; whoever takes it rightfully is blessed in it, and whoever takes it wrongfully is like one who eats and is never satiated; woe to the one who plunges into the wealth of Allah and His Messenger from the punishment of Hell on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Habib ibn Abi Thabit except Ismail ibn Muslim, nor from Ismail except Abu Bahr; Abu Burayd is alone in narrating it."
"8368","8368 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yusuf al-Samti narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cheats us is not of us. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Sa'd except Yusuf ibn Khalid; his son is alone in narrating it."
"8369","8369 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Abu Shihab al-Hannat narrated to us, from Hamzah ibn Abi Hamzah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The noblest of sittings are those faced toward the qiblah. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi' except Hamzah ibn Abi Hamzah."
"8370","8370 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Azhar ibn Marwan al-Raqashi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Rashid narrated to us, Sa'id al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu al-Ala ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah tests the servant to see how he acts; if he is content he is blessed, and if he is not content he is not blessed. No one narrated this hadith from al-Jurayri except Sa'id ibn Rashid; Azhar ibn Marwan is alone in narrating it."
"8371","8371 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Azhar ibn Marwan narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ata ibn Abi Maymunah narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Abi Wahshiyyah narrated to us, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning wiping over the khuffs: for the traveller three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ma'shar except Rawh ibn Ata; Azhar ibn Marwan is alone in narrating it."
"8372","8372 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Mu'awiyah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the mu'adhdhin and repeated as he said, until he said: Come to prayer - then he said: There is no power nor strength except through Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Amr except Ibn Uyaynah; Ahmad ibn Thabit is alone in narrating it."
"8373","8373 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Hammad narrated to us, from Sayf al-Usaydi, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar and Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The first to accept Islam was Abu Bakr. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd Allah and Musa except Sayf, nor from Sayf except al-Nadr ibn Hammad."
"8374","8374 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Hammad narrated to us, Sayf al-Usaydi narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see those who revile my Companions, say: May Allah curse the worst of you. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd Allah except Sayf; al-Nadr is alone in narrating it."
"8375","8375 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khulayd al-Hanafi narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Muharib ibn Dithar who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The false witness - his feet shall not move on the Day of Resurrection until the Fire becomes due for him."
"8376","8376 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik: That he was ten years old when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah. He said: My mothers used to urge me to serve the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ten years of his life in Madinah; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died when I was twenty years old. He said: I was the most knowledgeable of people concerning the matter of the hijab when it was revealed; Ubayy ibn Ka'b used to ask me about it. He said: The first of it was revealed when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) consummated his marriage with Zaynab bint Jahsh; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke with her as a bride, invited the people who ate of the food, then they left while some of them remained with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), prolonging their stay. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and went out, and I went out with him so that they would leave; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked and I walked with him until he came to the threshold of Aishah's chamber; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked to see whether they had left, then returned and I returned with him until he entered upon Zaynab, and they had left; then a screen was placed between me and them, and the verse of hijab was revealed. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri in this complete form except Yunus; Hassan ibn Ibrahim is alone in narrating it."
"8377","8377 - Musa ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Firas Abu Hurayrah al-Sayrafi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Wazir narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from his father, from Shaybah al-Hajabi, from his uncle who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things make your brother's love sincere to you: you greet him when you meet him, you make room for him in sittings, and you call him by the names most beloved to him. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Abd al-Malik except Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Wazir."
"8378","8378 - Musa ibn Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Bahili narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Sahl al-Raqashi narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever is not content with the decree and foreordainment of Allah, let him seek a god other than Him. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid al-Hadhdha except Ziyad ibn Sahl."
"8379","8379 - Musa ibn Sahl Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim informed us, Abd Allah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr narrated to us, that he heard al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman narrating from Abu Umamah, in marfu' form, who said: The Greatest Name of Allah, by which if He is invoked He answers, is in three surahs: al-Baqarah, Al Imran, and Ta-Ha. No one narrated this hadith from Abd Allah ibn al-Ala except al-Walid; Hisham is alone in narrating it."
"8380","8380 - Musa ibn Sahl narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ata, from Abd al-Malik ibn Jabir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which of the two terms did Musa fulfill? He said: The fuller of them. This hadith is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in narrating it."
"8381","8381 - Musa ibn Sahl narrated to us, Isa ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas, al-Layth ibn Sa'd, Ibn Abi al-Zinad and Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to them, from his father, from Aishah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three white Yemeni Sahuli garments with neither shirt nor turban, wrapped in them wrapping. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn al-Harith except Ibn Wahb."
"8382","8382 - Musa ibn Sahl narrated to us, Isa ibn Hammad narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Madani narrated to him, that Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to him, that Aishah informed him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have intercourse then wake junub, then bathe and fast. No one narrated this hadith from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman, who is Abu Tuwalah, from Abu Salamah except Amr; while Malik ibn Anas narrated it from Abu Tuwalah from Abu Yunus, freedman of Aishah, from Aishah."
"8383","8383 - Musa ibn Sahl narrated to us, Isa ibn Hammad narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj narrated to him, that Abd Allah ibn Abi Salamah narrated to him, from al-Nu'man ibn Abi Ayyash, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade leasing land."
"8384","8384 - Bukayr said: And Nafi' narrated to me that he heard Ibn Umar say: We used to lease land, then we abandoned that when we heard the hadith of Rafi' ibn Khadij from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated these two hadiths from Bukayr except Amr; Ibn Wahb is alone in narrating them."
"8385","8385 - Musa ibn Sahl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rumh narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked a man: Where did you stay? He said: With so-and-so woman. He said: Did she close her door upon you? He said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked that."
"8386","8386 - Musa ibn Sahl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rumh narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man shall enter upon a woman except with a mahram present with her. No one narrated these two hadiths from Khalid ibn Yazid except Ibn Lahi'ah."
"8387","8387 - Musa ibn Sahl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rumh narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Had, that Muslim ibn al-Walid ibn Rabah informed him, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: It is not lawful for a woman to fast in the presence of her husband except with his permission; whatever she gives in charity from his earnings, half of it is his; she is from a rib - if you treat her gently you enjoy her, and if you try to straighten her you break her, and her breaking is her separation. No one narrated this hadith from Muslim except Ibn al-Had; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in narrating it."
"8388","8388 - Musa ibn Sahl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rumh narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, that Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman informed him, from Yazid, freedman of al-Munba'ith, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a lost sheep. He said: It is for you, your brother, or the wolf. Then he asked him about a lost camel. He said: What have you to do with a lost camel? It has its shoes and its water-skin; it comes to water and eats trees - leave it until its owner finds it. No one narrated this hadith from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah except Ibn Lahi'ah; Muhammad ibn Rumh is alone in narrating it."
"8389","8389 - Musa ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abu Taqi Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, al-Mu'afa ibn Imran al-Tujibi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid al-Ayli, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seeking knowledge is obligatory upon every Muslim. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Yunus, nor from Yunus except Ismail, nor from Ismail except al-Mu'afa; Abu Taqi is alone in narrating it."
"8390","8390 - Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rumh narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Abu Abd Allah, freedman of Shaddad ibn al-Had, informed him, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man announcing a lost item in the mosque and said: May you not find it; say: May you not find it - mosques were not built for this. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Abd Allah, freedman of Shaddad ibn al-Had, except Abu al-Aswad; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in narrating it."
"8391","8391 - Musa ibn Sahl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rumh narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn al-Muhajir ibn Qunfudh al-Taymi, that he heard Abu Ghatfan ibn Tarif al-Murri reporting from Sa'id ibn Zayd who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever takes a handspan of a Muslim man's right unjustly, Allah will yoke him with seven earths on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ghatfan except Muhammad ibn Zayd, nor from Muhammad ibn Zayd except Ibn Lahi'ah and Hisham ibn Sa'd."
"8392","8392 - Musa ibn Sahl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rumh narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, that Abu al-Khayr narrated to him, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, you send us and we pass by people and ask them for hospitality and they refuse us; what shall we do, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Ask them for the guest's due which is his right; if they refuse it, take from them even if they dislike it - evil people are a people who do not honor the guest. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Abi Habib except Ibn Lahi'ah."
"8393","8393 - Musa ibn Sahl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rumh narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib and Abd Allah ibn Ziyad ibn Sam'an narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Ansari narrated to me, that a man peeped through a hole in the door of the house of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a midra with which he was scratching his head; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had we known you were looking at us, we would have stabbed it into your eye; permission was made only on account of sight."
"8394","8394 - Musa ibn Sahl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rumh narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, that he heard Urwah reporting from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Jews and Christians do not dye, so differ from them. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Aswad except Ibn Lahi'ah."
"8395","8395 - Musa ibn Sahl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rumh narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abd Rabbih ibn Sa'id, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The two traders have the choice until they part, or one gives the other choice and he chooses. No one narrated this hadith from Abd Rabbih except Ibn Lahi'ah."
"8396","8396 - Musa ibn Sahl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rumh narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, that Bukayr ibn Abd Allah informed him, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that after Abu Lubabah informed him from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of what he informed him, when he saw him he threatened him and stood up to him; sometimes he would order Nafi' to carry him until he cast him to the side of the houses. No one narrated this hadith from Bukayr except Yazid ibn Abi Habib; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in narrating it."
"8397","8397 - Musa ibn Sahl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rumh narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far, from Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: People spoke much about Friday ghusl, yet that was in my house and with me: Some people of the Awali entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when they came from there, while people then wore wool; he smelled an odor from them and said: Would that when this day comes you bathe. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr except Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far."
"8398","8398 - And with the same chain, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far, from Ammar ibn Abi Farwah, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever sells palm trees after pollinating them, their fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates otherwise. No one narrated this hadith from Ammar ibn Abi Farwah except Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in narrating it."
"8399","8399 - And with the same chain, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade one of you to outbid his brother until he abandons, except spoils and inheritances, and that one of you propose over the proposal of his brother until he abandons. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in narrating it, and 'except spoils and inheritances' is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"8400","8400 - And with the same chain: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no harm in a man selling his ariyyah of palm trees for its estimated measure of dates, meaning: for the other to eat it. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far except Ibn Lahi'ah."
